WEBVTT

00:02:15.230 --> 00:02:16.610
Morning, bro.

00:02:18.420 --> 00:02:20.110
I told you to stop calling me that.

00:02:20.110 --> 00:02:21.870
Sorry, Haru.

00:02:22.390 --> 00:02:24.140
We'll be late for the entrance ceremony.

00:02:27.750 --> 00:02:28.750
Boys' Locker Room

00:02:28.750 --> 00:02:30.630
Boys' Locker Room

00:02:47.890 --> 00:02:50.650
Haru, you need to button up your collar!

00:02:51.770 --> 00:02:52.880
It's too tight.

00:02:52.880 --> 00:02:54.690
You'll get used to it in no time.

00:03:03.610 --> 00:03:05.500
How did you know where I was going to be?

00:03:08.680 --> 00:03:10.710
I know everything about you, Haru.

00:03:12.290 --> 00:03:15.870
Well, maybe not everything.
Your mom told me where you were.

00:03:17.450 --> 00:03:18.240
I see.

00:03:20.020 --> 00:03:22.540
Are you going to join a club?

00:03:22.540 --> 00:03:23.550
I'm...

00:03:27.930 --> 00:03:29.900
I mean, are you gonna? I haven't decided yet.

00:03:31.300 --> 00:03:32.270
"Gonna"?

00:03:32.740 --> 00:03:38.860
Since we're in middle school now, I thought I'd try to sound older.

00:05:05.880 --> 00:05:07.070
Oh, I see me!

00:05:07.440 --> 00:05:08.570
I'm in Class 2.

00:05:09.670 --> 00:05:11.300
Can you not see it?

00:05:11.300 --> 00:05:12.990
You're in...

00:05:18.280 --> 00:05:20.370
I guess we're in different classes.

00:05:23.620 --> 00:05:27.840
Our rooms are right next door,
so we'll be together for joint lessons and P.E.

00:05:28.200 --> 00:05:29.370
That's true, but still—

00:05:29.370 --> 00:05:31.000
Tachibana!

00:05:31.000 --> 00:05:32.740
Oh, Mochizuki?

00:05:32.740 --> 00:05:34.670
Hey! I'm in Class 2 too!

00:05:34.670 --> 00:05:35.980
Oh, really?

00:05:35.980 --> 00:05:37.210
Yeah!

00:05:37.210 --> 00:05:40.470
We haven't been in the same class since third grade, huh?

00:05:41.510 --> 00:05:43.230
Wait, Haru!

00:05:47.370 --> 00:05:49.490
Hey! Wanna join the swim club?

00:05:49.790 --> 00:05:51.810
No, I'm not...

00:05:51.810 --> 00:05:53.340
What? It's fine!

00:05:53.340 --> 00:05:55.120
Let's swim together!

00:05:55.120 --> 00:05:58.080
Unless you've already decided what club to join?

00:05:58.080 --> 00:05:59.250
Not yet, but...

00:05:59.250 --> 00:06:00.500
What's the problem, then?

00:06:00.500 --> 00:06:01.580
Let's swim!

00:06:01.580 --> 00:06:06.400
No, I haven't decided which one yet,
but I was thinking of joining a cultural club.

00:06:07.640 --> 00:06:09.590
Are you Nanase Haruka?

00:06:11.110 --> 00:06:12.720
I'm Shigino Kisumi.

00:06:12.720 --> 00:06:14.580
I went to Sano Elementary,

00:06:14.580 --> 00:06:18.100
and I heard about you from Matsuoka Rin.

00:06:18.520 --> 00:06:19.470
From Rin?

00:06:19.470 --> 00:06:23.230
He said there was this really fast guy at Iwatobi Swimming Club.

00:06:23.230 --> 00:06:24.900
"Swimming Club"?!

00:06:25.310 --> 00:06:27.290
You go to an SC?

00:06:27.290 --> 00:06:28.410
"SC"?

00:06:28.410 --> 00:06:30.410
It's short for "swimming club"!

00:06:30.780 --> 00:06:32.410
I'm Shiina Asahi.

00:06:32.410 --> 00:06:34.460
Um... Nanase!

00:06:34.460 --> 00:06:37.730
You're definitely joining the swim club, right?

00:06:37.730 --> 00:06:38.820
Right?

00:06:38.820 --> 00:06:40.120
I haven't decided yet.

00:06:40.120 --> 00:06:41.750
What, you haven't decided yet?

00:06:42.100 --> 00:06:44.840
In that case, wanna join the basketball club with me?

00:06:44.840 --> 00:06:47.170
Hey, you can't just steal him like that!

00:06:47.170 --> 00:06:49.070
Join the swim club! Okay?

00:06:49.070 --> 00:06:52.890
If you're already going to a swimming club,
then you don't need to swim any more, do you?

00:06:52.890 --> 00:06:54.090
So join the basketball club.

00:06:54.090 --> 00:06:55.180
Shut up!

00:07:00.270 --> 00:07:03.370
The picture from back then got put up, huh?

00:07:06.320 --> 00:07:08.750
I wonder what Rin's doing now.

00:07:08.750 --> 00:07:09.630
Who knows?

00:07:12.620 --> 00:07:14.910
Haru, Mako!

00:07:14.910 --> 00:07:17.630
Nagisa, it's not safe to run out here.

00:07:17.630 --> 00:07:19.620
Oh, sorry.

00:07:19.620 --> 00:07:22.200
Hey, how's middle school going?

00:07:22.200 --> 00:07:23.480
Is it fun?

00:07:23.480 --> 00:07:25.800
It's hard to say after just one day.

00:07:25.800 --> 00:07:26.670
It's normal.

00:07:26.670 --> 00:07:28.030
Really?

00:07:28.860 --> 00:07:32.900
I wish I was in the same grade as you guys.

00:07:32.900 --> 00:07:36.430
You'll be a middle schooler too next year.

00:07:36.810 --> 00:07:41.200
But I can't be in the relay with you two this year, can I?

00:07:41.200 --> 00:07:42.850
And Rin's gone.

00:07:44.110 --> 00:07:45.410
Yeah.

00:07:55.260 --> 00:07:56.580
Hey, Haruka!

00:07:56.580 --> 00:07:58.290
Jumping in without permission again?!

00:08:02.360 --> 00:08:03.040
I'm home.

00:08:03.480 --> 00:08:04.560
Welcome back.

00:08:04.560 --> 00:08:06.330
Your school seems nice.

00:08:06.330 --> 00:08:07.870
How was your class?

00:08:07.870 --> 00:08:08.800
Normal.

00:08:08.800 --> 00:08:10.490
Really?

00:08:10.490 --> 00:08:12.510
Come down once you've changed.

00:08:12.510 --> 00:08:14.340
Dinner's already on the table.

00:08:14.340 --> 00:08:14.800
'Kay.

00:08:32.820 --> 00:08:34.320
Club Application Form

00:08:36.160 --> 00:08:38.700
<i>I'm not going to a middle school around here.</i>

00:08:40.200 --> 00:08:41.950
I'm going to Australia.

00:08:42.280 --> 00:08:43.960
I'm gonna become an Olympic swimmer.

00:08:50.170 --> 00:08:53.020
Flying trapeze!

00:08:59.600 --> 00:09:02.160
Ikuya, how's school?

00:09:04.880 --> 00:09:06.350
I can't really tell yet.

00:09:06.350 --> 00:09:07.910
I see.

00:09:10.230 --> 00:09:11.520
Thanks for dinner.

00:09:11.520 --> 00:09:13.250
Really? You barely ate.

00:09:13.250 --> 00:09:13.960
Yeah.

00:09:32.680 --> 00:09:35.380
Asahi, what're you doi—

00:09:37.690 --> 00:09:39.640
Sis, don't laugh!

00:09:42.350 --> 00:09:43.760
I'm heading out!

00:09:50.430 --> 00:09:51.270
Coming!

00:09:51.960 --> 00:09:54.350
Morning, Mrs. Nanase.

00:09:54.350 --> 00:09:56.260
Morning, Makoto.

00:09:56.260 --> 00:09:57.530
Haruka!

00:09:57.820 --> 00:09:59.560
Makoto's here!

00:10:00.700 --> 00:10:01.490
'Kay.

00:10:01.870 --> 00:10:03.130
Morning, Haru.

00:10:04.520 --> 00:10:06.000
Let's go, Makoto.

00:10:07.640 --> 00:10:09.040
Jeez...

00:10:13.950 --> 00:10:15.510
Nanase! Run!

00:10:17.990 --> 00:10:18.930
I'm open!

00:10:21.520 --> 00:10:22.140
Nanase!

00:10:26.960 --> 00:10:28.310
Okay, all done!

00:10:28.310 --> 00:10:29.720
Finally!

00:10:28.780 --> 00:10:30.980
I need to work hard too.

00:10:29.720 --> 00:10:30.980
That was a good shot.

00:10:32.570 --> 00:10:35.030
That last shot was amazing.

00:10:35.470 --> 00:10:38.430
You stopped pretty much all my other shots, though.

00:10:39.760 --> 00:10:41.620
Nanase!

00:10:43.240 --> 00:10:46.090
Oh, you're the kid from Class 2 who was killing it!

00:10:46.090 --> 00:10:47.000
Um...

00:10:47.390 --> 00:10:48.710
Tachibana?

00:10:50.220 --> 00:10:52.210
I'm Tachibana Makoto.

00:10:52.210 --> 00:10:53.130
Nice to meet you.

00:10:53.590 --> 00:10:54.820
Yeah, nice to meet you!

00:10:54.820 --> 00:10:56.420
I'm Shiina Asahi.

00:10:56.420 --> 00:10:58.970
I'm Shigino Kisumi. Nice to meet you!

00:10:59.510 --> 00:11:02.850
Hey, what'd you think of my rebounds?

00:11:03.130 --> 00:11:04.560
They were cool.

00:11:05.670 --> 00:11:06.600
Really?

00:11:06.600 --> 00:11:09.250
Well, I can do pretty much anything, you know.

00:11:09.250 --> 00:11:12.030
Which is exactly why you should join the basketball club!

00:11:12.030 --> 00:11:16.030
I'm not joining! Nanase and I have the swim club!

00:11:16.030 --> 00:11:16.570
Right?

00:11:16.910 --> 00:11:19.010
What? You're joining the swim club?

00:11:19.010 --> 00:11:20.690
I never said I was joining.

00:11:20.690 --> 00:11:22.300
You should join, Makoto.

00:11:22.300 --> 00:11:22.910
What?

00:11:23.300 --> 00:11:26.120
Don't tell me you go to the same SC as Nanase?!

00:11:26.120 --> 00:11:27.550
Huh? Yeah.

00:11:27.550 --> 00:11:29.410
You're joining the swim club too, then!

00:11:29.410 --> 00:11:30.120
Why?!

00:11:30.120 --> 00:11:32.830
Aw, join the basketball club.

00:11:32.830 --> 00:11:34.530
Right, Nanase?

00:11:34.530 --> 00:11:36.620
Haru, you're so popular.

00:11:37.300 --> 00:11:38.420
"Haru"?

00:11:38.420 --> 00:11:40.440
Oh, because your first name's "Haruka"?

00:11:40.440 --> 00:11:43.160
Can I call you guys "Haru" and "Makoto" too?

00:11:43.160 --> 00:11:44.890
You're so shameless.

00:11:44.890 --> 00:11:45.970
I don't care.

00:11:45.500 --> 00:11:45.970
Sure.

00:11:46.280 --> 00:11:47.130
Hey!

00:11:47.130 --> 00:11:48.380
It's okay?!

00:11:48.380 --> 00:11:51.080
I'm calling you guys "Haru"
and "Makoto" too, in that case!

00:11:51.080 --> 00:11:52.200
Do what you want.

00:11:52.200 --> 00:11:52.980
It's fine.

00:11:56.100 --> 00:11:58.230
You can just call me "Asahi" too!

00:11:58.590 --> 00:12:02.740
Nice to meet you all again, Haru, Makoto, Asahi.

00:12:02.740 --> 00:12:04.850
I didn't say you could!

00:12:04.850 --> 00:12:07.640
It's fine, isn't it? You can just call me "Kisumi" too.

00:12:07.640 --> 00:12:11.000
Oh my, he just said "kiss me"! What a pervy name!

00:12:11.320 --> 00:12:14.110
You're the pervy one for even thinking of it like that.

00:12:14.730 --> 00:12:15.630
Pervert.

00:12:15.980 --> 00:12:17.630
I'm not a pervert!

00:12:17.630 --> 00:12:18.860
Don't call me that!

00:12:18.860 --> 00:12:19.920
Whatever.

00:12:32.020 --> 00:12:32.690
Hey.

00:12:53.610 --> 00:12:57.130
Haru, are you a little tired from the new school and everything?

00:12:57.130 --> 00:12:58.290
Not really.

00:12:58.290 --> 00:12:59.950
It's a little noisy.

00:12:59.950 --> 00:13:03.760
I bet it is. There are a lot of energetic kids in your class.

00:13:04.550 --> 00:13:07.950
Speaking of which, Kisumi asked us to join the basketball club, right?

00:13:07.950 --> 00:13:09.840
Did you decide on a club yet?

00:13:09.840 --> 00:13:11.270
I haven't yet.

00:13:11.270 --> 00:13:15.390
Our school requires you to join a club, you know.

00:13:15.880 --> 00:13:17.650
What about you?

00:13:17.650 --> 00:13:18.720
Me?

00:13:21.300 --> 00:13:22.650
I haven't decided yet.

00:13:23.190 --> 00:13:24.900
Then stop worrying about me.

00:13:24.900 --> 00:13:27.780
There are a lot of different clubs, so it's hard to decide, huh?

00:13:30.310 --> 00:13:31.620
How about the basketball club?

00:13:32.080 --> 00:13:32.580
Huh?

00:13:38.710 --> 00:13:39.840
Makoto?

00:13:39.840 --> 00:13:40.710
Are you...

00:13:41.210 --> 00:13:44.090
okay with me joining the basketball club?

00:13:48.380 --> 00:13:50.970
You're free to decide which club you join.

00:13:55.600 --> 00:13:56.730
You're right.

00:13:57.080 --> 00:13:58.910
Basketball, huh?

00:13:58.910 --> 00:14:01.110
I've only ever played it in P.E.,

00:14:01.110 --> 00:14:02.950
but I don't think that's a problem.

00:14:09.440 --> 00:14:10.120
Are you...

00:14:10.550 --> 00:14:13.200
okay with me joining the basketball club?

00:14:20.060 --> 00:14:20.920
Haru!

00:14:20.920 --> 00:14:22.500
Let's eat together!

00:14:22.500 --> 00:14:25.160
I mean, I'm gonna eat here even if you say no.

00:14:25.160 --> 00:14:27.130
Haru, let's eat lunch!

00:14:27.130 --> 00:14:29.130
Wait, why are you here?

00:14:29.130 --> 00:14:31.330
It's fine! Let's all eat together!

00:14:31.330 --> 00:14:33.930
Shut up! I'm gonna eat lunch with Haru.

00:14:33.930 --> 00:14:36.350
Come on, don't be so stubborn.

00:14:36.890 --> 00:14:39.730
Hey, what elementary school did you go to, Asahi?

00:14:40.090 --> 00:14:43.730
You weren't at mine, and Haru,
you went to Iwatobi Elementary, right?

00:14:44.320 --> 00:14:47.380
Oh, I transferred here in March.

00:14:47.380 --> 00:14:49.610
So I didn't go to elementary school around here.

00:14:50.040 --> 00:14:52.600
Really? Did you swim back there too?

00:14:52.600 --> 00:14:53.580
You betcha!

00:14:53.580 --> 00:14:59.140
At my old SC, I swam the 50m and
100m butterfly, and the medley relay.

00:14:59.140 --> 00:15:00.830
What's a "medley relay"?

00:15:00.830 --> 00:15:02.730
It's when four people swim...

00:15:02.730 --> 00:15:03.810
Backstroke!

00:15:03.810 --> 00:15:04.920
Breaststroke!

00:15:04.920 --> 00:15:06.120
Butterfly!

00:15:06.120 --> 00:15:07.560
And freestyle!

00:15:07.560 --> 00:15:10.180
In a relay with different strokes!

00:15:10.710 --> 00:15:13.350
Anyway, if you don't know,
don't butt into our conversation!

00:15:13.650 --> 00:15:16.440
Even though you're mad,
you're still explaining it properly.

00:15:16.440 --> 00:15:17.980
You're a nice guy, huh?

00:15:19.510 --> 00:15:23.690
Well, I mean, just explaining doesn't cost me anything.

00:15:25.220 --> 00:15:27.220
I wanna compete at a swim meet...

00:15:27.220 --> 00:15:30.430
Oh, but I'd have a different
medley relay team, wouldn't I?

00:15:30.430 --> 00:15:34.410
I wanted to compete with the guys from my old SC.

00:15:41.540 --> 00:15:42.320
What?

00:15:42.320 --> 00:15:44.770
Are you both obsessed with swimming?

00:15:44.770 --> 00:15:46.770
Why not give basketball a chance?

00:15:46.770 --> 00:15:49.420
I told you, we're not joining the basketball club.

00:15:49.830 --> 00:15:54.620
I was thinking that we could be a good team in three years if we joined now.

00:15:54.620 --> 00:15:55.890
Are you looking down on me?

00:15:56.470 --> 00:15:59.180
If I join, I'll obviously be a starter right away!

00:15:59.180 --> 00:16:01.420
Wow, amazing! Amazing!

00:16:01.420 --> 00:16:02.930
You're so cool, Asahi.

00:16:02.930 --> 00:16:04.400
Just sign here.

00:16:04.400 --> 00:16:05.150
Sure thing!

00:16:04.400 --> 00:16:05.150
Club Application Form

00:16:04.400 --> 00:16:05.150
Name

00:16:04.400 --> 00:16:05.150
Shii

00:16:05.430 --> 00:16:06.400
I mean, hey!

00:16:06.860 --> 00:16:08.880
I told you, I'm not joining!

00:16:08.880 --> 00:16:09.580
Sorry, sorry!

00:16:09.580 --> 00:16:10.700
I almost started signing!

00:16:10.700 --> 00:16:11.490
Haru!

00:16:10.700 --> 00:16:12.740
Come on, join!

00:16:11.490 --> 00:16:12.740
Damn you!

00:16:21.580 --> 00:16:23.480
What is it, Makoto?

00:16:23.480 --> 00:16:25.830
Well, this third-year wanted to...

00:16:25.830 --> 00:16:29.890
Hey! You're Nanase Haruka from Iwatobi SC, right?

00:16:29.890 --> 00:16:31.340
Join the swim club.

00:16:34.480 --> 00:16:36.350
He's been like this for a while.

00:16:36.630 --> 00:16:38.030
Oh, right.

00:16:38.030 --> 00:16:40.100
You can't tell like this, huh? Sorry.

00:16:40.600 --> 00:16:42.400
I'm Kirishima Natsuya.

00:16:42.400 --> 00:16:47.190
I'm the captain of the swim club,
and I came to invite you two to join.

00:16:47.190 --> 00:16:48.100
Again?

00:16:48.100 --> 00:16:49.860
Huh? I hope I didn't upset you.

00:16:50.480 --> 00:16:51.800
Nah, you're good.

00:16:51.800 --> 00:16:53.620
Speak politely!

00:16:53.620 --> 00:16:54.070
Sir.

00:16:55.750 --> 00:16:56.700
Well, how about it?

00:16:56.700 --> 00:16:58.450
Feel like joining the swim club?

00:16:59.400 --> 00:17:01.580
Haru, what should we do?

00:17:01.580 --> 00:17:02.460
Not interested.

00:17:02.460 --> 00:17:03.580
Haru!

00:17:03.960 --> 00:17:06.210
Have you already decided what club you're joining?

00:17:06.210 --> 00:17:08.030
Not yet, sir.

00:17:08.030 --> 00:17:10.990
We don't have many first-years joining,
so we're in a pinch.

00:17:10.990 --> 00:17:12.150
Please?

00:17:12.830 --> 00:17:14.480
What should we do?

00:17:15.480 --> 00:17:17.580
Everyone just messes around during practice, right?

00:17:21.060 --> 00:17:23.930
Ikuya, it isn't just fun and games.

00:17:23.930 --> 00:17:25.200
Yes, it is.

00:17:25.200 --> 00:17:29.060
What? You got tired of competing, so now you're trying to make new friends in some lame club?

00:17:29.620 --> 00:17:31.190
Leave it to my brother to be that stupid.

00:17:32.810 --> 00:17:34.240
You're brothers?

00:17:34.240 --> 00:17:35.950
Oh, uh, yeah.

00:17:36.710 --> 00:17:39.490
Anyway, think about joining the club, you two.

00:17:39.490 --> 00:17:40.090
Later.

00:17:40.090 --> 00:17:41.330
Huh? Wai—

00:17:43.270 --> 00:17:45.530
He said they don't have many new members.

00:17:45.530 --> 00:17:47.180
What should we do?

00:17:48.490 --> 00:17:50.300
You're too nice.

00:17:50.300 --> 00:17:53.040
Everyone says that when they're trying to get people to join.

00:17:53.040 --> 00:17:55.250
You think so?

00:17:55.250 --> 00:17:57.220
There's no need for you to join.

00:17:57.660 --> 00:17:59.970
You're Kirishima, right?

00:17:59.970 --> 00:18:01.770
Why do you think that?

00:18:01.770 --> 00:18:04.100
Everyone just messes around during practice.

00:18:04.590 --> 00:18:08.530
For someone like me who swims seriously at an SC,

00:18:08.530 --> 00:18:09.860
a school club is a waste of time.

00:18:10.390 --> 00:18:12.360
Don't you guys think so too?

00:18:12.360 --> 00:18:14.040
Not really.

00:18:14.040 --> 00:18:15.320
It's just a pain.

00:18:15.320 --> 00:18:17.200
They're just messing around!

00:18:19.400 --> 00:18:22.830
Anyway, I just can't take school clubs seriously.

00:18:24.030 --> 00:18:26.220
You're not gonna finish eating?

00:18:26.220 --> 00:18:28.290
Huh? You guys talking about something serious?

00:18:31.000 --> 00:18:34.610
Oh, you're the guy who's always sneaking glances at me!

00:18:34.610 --> 00:18:36.010
What?! I don't look at you!

00:18:36.010 --> 00:18:37.460
Yes, you do.

00:18:37.460 --> 00:18:40.990
What, you wanna be my friend that badly?

00:18:40.990 --> 00:18:42.360
What a shame.

00:18:42.360 --> 00:18:42.850
No.

00:18:43.530 --> 00:18:45.400
It leaks out even if I try to hide it, huh?

00:18:45.400 --> 00:18:46.270
What does?

00:18:46.270 --> 00:18:47.730
All this charisma.

00:18:47.730 --> 00:18:48.840
That's not it!

00:18:48.840 --> 00:18:51.690
It's because looking at you makes me laugh,
like I'm at a zoo!

00:18:51.690 --> 00:18:53.000
A zoo?

00:18:53.000 --> 00:18:53.650
Why?

00:18:54.900 --> 00:18:56.030
You remind me of a monkey.

00:18:59.080 --> 00:19:00.860
K-Kisumi, don't laugh!

00:19:00.860 --> 00:19:02.770
I'm mad at you now!

00:19:02.770 --> 00:19:04.790
If you think I'm a monkey, then you're the monkey!

00:19:05.100 --> 00:19:07.170
I-It's fine, Asahi!

00:19:07.170 --> 00:19:09.960
All humans come from monkeys.

00:19:09.960 --> 00:19:11.920
Whose side are you on?!

00:19:12.360 --> 00:19:15.550
See. He's screeching just like a monkey, isn't he?

00:19:14.800 --> 00:19:15.550
You're all too loud.

00:19:17.930 --> 00:19:18.550
Oh!

00:19:18.550 --> 00:19:21.560
One, two, three, four, five!

00:19:21.560 --> 00:19:22.410
Huh?

00:19:22.410 --> 00:19:23.860
We have exactly five people.

00:19:23.860 --> 00:19:26.010
Wanna join the basketball club together?

00:19:26.010 --> 00:19:27.530
I'm not joining.

00:19:28.950 --> 00:19:30.140
You're still saying that?

00:19:30.140 --> 00:19:33.860
'Cause what club are you guys gonna join instead?

00:19:33.860 --> 00:19:35.860
The swim club, of course!

00:19:35.860 --> 00:19:37.860
I still haven't decided.

00:19:38.270 --> 00:19:38.990
I'm not interested.

00:19:38.990 --> 00:19:39.990
Same here.

00:19:39.990 --> 00:19:40.970
What?!

00:19:40.970 --> 00:19:44.620
I don't know about this guy,
but Haru and Makoto are joining the swim club, right?!

00:19:44.620 --> 00:19:45.700
You're both swimmers, right?!

00:19:46.200 --> 00:19:47.560
So you should join!

00:19:47.560 --> 00:19:49.010
How'd you end up there?

00:19:49.010 --> 00:19:52.580
If we follow your logic,
then everyone who can swim would have to join.

00:19:52.580 --> 00:19:53.770
Wait.

00:19:53.770 --> 00:19:56.460
Why did I get put in the "can't swim" category?

00:19:56.460 --> 00:19:59.020
Oh, you can swim?

00:19:59.020 --> 00:20:01.680
I've been going to Bandou SC since first grade.

00:20:00.970 --> 00:20:04.330
Oh, Kirishima, you swim too?

00:20:05.520 --> 00:20:08.930
That's why I'm not interested in a club that won't take swimming seriously.

00:20:08.930 --> 00:20:09.730
What?

00:20:09.730 --> 00:20:11.810
How do you know they won't take it seriously?

00:20:12.470 --> 00:20:15.560
In clubs, they don't split you into teams based on ability,

00:20:15.560 --> 00:20:18.250
and all the practice is way too easy.

00:20:18.250 --> 00:20:20.610
Everyone's just screwing around.

00:20:21.670 --> 00:20:23.070
What'd you say?!

00:20:23.480 --> 00:20:25.160
You don't know that!

00:20:25.520 --> 00:20:29.120
You haven't joined yet, so how would you know?!

00:20:29.120 --> 00:20:31.120
I don't! That's why I'm joining!

00:20:32.290 --> 00:20:34.750
How are you supposed to know without doing it?!

00:20:36.150 --> 00:20:38.750
Aren't you just scared?

00:20:40.580 --> 00:20:41.420
What did you say?

00:20:41.830 --> 00:20:45.410
You're scared of jumping into something new, aren't you?

00:20:46.590 --> 00:20:47.720
Oh no.

00:20:48.220 --> 00:20:50.470
I forgot to give those guys a swim club flyer.

00:20:50.470 --> 00:20:52.790
Nao would be mad if he found out.

00:20:53.950 --> 00:20:54.770
Fine!

00:20:54.770 --> 00:20:58.440
If you're gonna go that far, then I'll join and prove to you that no one takes it seriously!

00:21:00.030 --> 00:21:02.150
Oh, sorry.

00:21:02.150 --> 00:21:04.000
Kirishima?

00:21:04.000 --> 00:21:06.030
I forgot to give these to you earlier.

00:21:06.390 --> 00:21:08.930
Here.

00:21:08.930 --> 00:21:10.490
Swim club flyer?

00:21:10.490 --> 00:21:12.460
Oh, I'm joining the basketball club.

00:21:12.460 --> 00:21:13.970
Aw, too bad.

00:21:13.970 --> 00:21:15.760
Everyone here will join!

00:21:15.760 --> 00:21:16.730
Other than Kisumi!

00:21:16.730 --> 00:21:17.800
Wait, seriously?

00:21:17.800 --> 00:21:20.280
What? I'm the only one being left out?

00:21:20.280 --> 00:21:21.300
There's nothing to be left out of.

00:21:21.300 --> 00:21:22.720
Us too?

00:21:22.720 --> 00:21:24.160
We didn't agree to join yet.

00:21:24.160 --> 00:21:26.250
Haru, you say something too.

00:21:26.250 --> 00:21:27.600
It's better than basketball.

00:21:27.600 --> 00:21:29.140
I'm not sure that's a good reason.

00:21:29.140 --> 00:21:31.330
Don't knock basketball, you guys!

00:21:34.910 --> 00:21:36.650
Don't give up halfway through.

00:21:37.790 --> 00:21:39.200
I won't!

00:21:42.300 --> 00:21:45.240
Well, I'll see you at the pool after the Golden Week holidays!

00:21:47.450 --> 00:21:51.790
Aw man, in the end, the swim club took everyone.

00:21:52.250 --> 00:21:56.170
We ended up joining without really knowing what was going on, huh?

00:22:01.590 --> 00:22:02.940
Everyone, gather round!

00:22:02.940 --> 00:22:03.960
Yes, sir!

00:22:05.320 --> 00:22:07.340
We have new members as of today.

00:22:07.860 --> 00:22:10.200
I'm sure you second- and third-years know this,

00:22:10.200 --> 00:22:13.100
but we'll have a practice swim meet against Sano Middle School soon.

00:22:13.540 --> 00:22:15.420
An official meet will follow.

00:22:15.420 --> 00:22:18.050
First-years will also be participating, so stay focused.

00:22:18.050 --> 00:22:18.860
Yes, sir!

00:22:18.860 --> 00:22:19.600
Now...

00:22:20.430 --> 00:22:22.360
these are our new first-years.

00:22:23.030 --> 00:22:25.110
Okay, will you introduce yourselves starting from this end?

00:22:25.950 --> 00:22:27.860
Shiina Asahi, first-year!

00:22:28.200 --> 00:22:31.100
Hey, we already know you're a first-year.

00:22:31.100 --> 00:22:32.700
Oh, um...

00:22:33.200 --> 00:22:35.730
I just moved here in the spring!

00:22:35.730 --> 00:22:38.670
I was part of an SC where I used to live,
and I'm good at butterfly!

00:22:39.080 --> 00:22:41.180
I expect to get faster and faster!

00:22:41.180 --> 00:22:42.830
Thank you!

00:22:48.570 --> 00:22:50.140
Ikuya, introduce yourself.

00:22:51.230 --> 00:22:53.890
I'm Kirishima Ikuya. I swim breaststroke.

00:22:58.320 --> 00:22:59.770
I'm Tachibana Makoto.

00:22:59.770 --> 00:23:02.910
At Iwatobi SC, I swam backstroke.

00:23:02.910 --> 00:23:04.430
Thank you.

00:23:05.710 --> 00:23:06.990
Nanase Haruka.

00:23:06.990 --> 00:23:08.700
I only swim freestyle.

00:23:08.700 --> 00:23:10.220
Be polite, please.

00:23:10.960 --> 00:23:11.680
Thank you.

00:23:14.190 --> 00:23:17.740
Now that I think about it,
you guys all swim different strokes, huh?

00:23:17.740 --> 00:23:20.060
You can enter the first-year medley relay.

00:23:20.700 --> 00:23:22.650
I'll only swim in individual events.

00:23:22.650 --> 00:23:23.820
Sir.

00:23:23.820 --> 00:23:25.340
And I only swim freestyle.

00:23:25.720 --> 00:23:26.340
Huh?

00:23:27.690 --> 00:23:28.520
Haruka.

00:23:30.050 --> 00:23:31.340
Don't call me by my first name.

00:23:31.340 --> 00:23:33.710
What are you muttering about?

00:23:33.710 --> 00:23:37.020
More importantly, as captain, I won't let you say you'll only swim in individual events,

00:23:37.020 --> 00:23:39.100
and only freestyle at that.

00:23:39.720 --> 00:23:41.100
You won't do the relay no matter what?

00:23:45.230 --> 00:23:46.980
Haruka!

00:23:46.980 --> 00:23:48.860
Don't get too cocky, kid.

00:23:50.280 --> 00:23:51.840
Get in the pool right now.

00:23:52.490 --> 00:23:53.370
Come on.

00:23:53.880 --> 00:23:55.950
We're gonna have a 50m race.

00:23:57.260 --> 00:23:58.550
We'll swim...

00:23:59.690 --> 00:24:00.290
freestyle!

00:24:05.620 --> 00:24:08.060
U-Um, wait—

00:24:08.060 --> 00:24:10.510
Our captain won't listen to anyone after he gets like that.

00:24:10.510 --> 00:24:11.550
You might as well give up.

00:24:11.550 --> 00:24:12.780
What?

00:24:13.750 --> 00:24:17.850
Haruka, if you want to stick to your convictions, then earn them by winning.

00:24:18.330 --> 00:24:19.470
Stop using my first name.

00:24:19.470 --> 00:24:22.350
This isn't the time for that, Haru!

00:24:22.350 --> 00:24:23.550
Nao, you're the starter.

00:24:23.550 --> 00:24:24.370
Okay.

00:24:24.370 --> 00:24:25.690
On your marks...

00:24:27.580 --> 00:24:28.320
Get set...

00:24:40.120 --> 00:24:41.490
That kid's fast!

00:24:41.490 --> 00:24:42.750
He's as fast as the captain!

00:24:46.520 --> 00:24:47.040
Here's the turn!

00:24:48.470 --> 00:24:50.760
That first-year's still keeping up with the captain!

00:24:51.930 --> 00:24:52.970
They're neck and neck!

00:25:07.600 --> 00:25:09.150
You two were tied.

00:25:09.700 --> 00:25:10.850
I see.

00:25:10.850 --> 00:25:12.010
Damn it!

00:25:16.040 --> 00:25:18.330
You really are fast.

00:25:18.330 --> 00:25:20.960
Fine, you can just swim freestyle.

00:25:20.960 --> 00:25:24.370
But it was a tie, so I'll have you in the relay too.

00:25:28.590 --> 00:25:30.460
Next time we race, I'll win!

00:25:38.790 --> 00:25:39.560
Haru.

00:25:39.560 --> 00:25:41.810
All right, let's start practice!

00:25:41.810 --> 00:25:42.810
Yes, sir!

00:25:44.430 --> 00:25:45.860
You're fast.

00:25:45.860 --> 00:25:46.600
I'm normal.

00:25:46.600 --> 00:25:48.340
Th-That was great!

00:25:48.340 --> 00:25:50.300
I was so surprised!

00:25:50.300 --> 00:25:52.570
Come on, first-years are over here!

00:25:52.570 --> 00:25:53.950
Yes, sir.

00:25:55.160 --> 00:25:57.010
This is Serizawa Nao, a third-year.

00:25:57.010 --> 00:25:59.660
He's mainly a manager.

00:25:59.660 --> 00:26:03.840
He's also in charge of coaching the first-years, so you'll learn from him.

00:26:03.840 --> 00:26:04.660
Yes, sir!

00:26:05.100 --> 00:26:06.190
Nice to meet you.

00:26:06.190 --> 00:26:08.670
Asahi, Ikuya, Makoto,

00:26:08.980 --> 00:26:10.060
Haruka.

00:26:10.060 --> 00:26:11.420
My first name again.

00:26:11.870 --> 00:26:14.610
Do you really hate being called by your first name that much?

00:26:14.610 --> 00:26:16.490
Too bad for you.

00:26:16.490 --> 00:26:18.680
All club members call each other by first name!

00:26:18.680 --> 00:26:19.960
That's our motto!

00:26:19.960 --> 00:26:20.840
What?

00:26:22.310 --> 00:26:23.140
That's right.

00:26:23.140 --> 00:26:27.320
Because swimmers usually compete as individuals, it can be easy to become self-centered.

00:26:27.320 --> 00:26:29.990
But that won't work for a club like ours.

00:26:29.990 --> 00:26:32.900
This way, we can form deeper bonds.

00:26:34.900 --> 00:26:36.890
Okay, Nao, I'm leaving the rest to you.

00:26:36.890 --> 00:26:37.920
Right.

00:26:37.920 --> 00:26:42.200
Now, I've been entrusted with coaching you guys,

00:26:42.200 --> 00:26:45.200
but I'll start things off by showing you around.

00:27:26.720 --> 00:27:30.890
All right, why don't we end with 200m across the pool?

00:27:31.840 --> 00:27:34.820
It'll be part of your cool-down,
so you don't have to go all-out.

00:27:34.820 --> 00:27:36.190
You'll be swimming freestyle.

00:27:36.190 --> 00:27:37.040
Yes, sir.

00:27:40.680 --> 00:27:41.680
Okay, next.

00:27:43.980 --> 00:27:45.150
Okay, next.

00:27:47.430 --> 00:27:48.610
Okay, next.

00:27:48.610 --> 00:27:49.680
Yessir.

00:28:03.190 --> 00:28:05.170
Come on, Asahi. Stop messing around.

00:28:06.090 --> 00:28:07.340
Sorry.

00:28:13.160 --> 00:28:14.300
What is it?

00:28:14.300 --> 00:28:15.290
Well...

00:28:23.510 --> 00:28:24.530
Asahi?

00:28:24.530 --> 00:28:26.140
What? Is this a joke?

00:28:27.420 --> 00:28:29.140
I...

00:28:29.670 --> 00:28:32.890
can't swim freestyle anymore!

00:28:33.240 --> 00:28:33.650
Huh?

00:28:34.200 --> 00:28:35.400
What?!

00:28:35.400 --> 00:28:37.110
Boys' Locker Room

00:28:37.640 --> 00:28:39.610
So you suddenly couldn't swim anymore?

00:28:40.060 --> 00:28:40.860
Yessir.

00:28:42.900 --> 00:28:45.900
Was it that you actually just couldn't swim freestyle?

00:28:46.600 --> 00:28:47.490
No, that's not it!

00:28:48.130 --> 00:28:49.700
I could!

00:28:49.700 --> 00:28:53.790
But... But today, when I tried, I couldn't.

00:28:56.490 --> 00:28:57.960
Why now out of nowhere?

00:28:57.960 --> 00:28:59.750
How should I know?!

00:28:59.750 --> 00:29:01.510
Maybe it's a mental issue.

00:29:02.590 --> 00:29:03.600
Mental?

00:29:06.120 --> 00:29:07.300
Don't worry.

00:29:07.750 --> 00:29:11.040
If you were able to swim it before,
then you'll be able to get the feel for it back in no time.

00:29:13.110 --> 00:29:13.770
Right!

00:29:21.360 --> 00:29:22.610
Ikuya!

00:29:22.950 --> 00:29:25.220
You're a lot better than you were earlier!

00:29:25.220 --> 00:29:26.360
Don't worry!

00:29:26.830 --> 00:29:30.210
You'll get the hang of it soon, so keep at it!

00:29:30.990 --> 00:29:32.050
Big Bro.

00:29:33.040 --> 00:29:33.910
Right!

00:29:37.680 --> 00:29:38.750
Hey, Ikuya!

00:29:39.180 --> 00:29:39.590
Ikuya!

00:29:41.630 --> 00:29:43.470
What's the deal with him?

00:29:48.490 --> 00:29:50.690
I wonder if Asahi will be okay.

00:29:50.690 --> 00:29:51.680
Who knows?

00:29:51.680 --> 00:29:55.370
Do you think Natsuya and Ikuya don't get along?

00:29:55.370 --> 00:29:56.140
Who knows?

00:29:56.630 --> 00:29:59.260
You're not even listening, are you?

00:30:01.270 --> 00:30:03.780
Yoo-hoo! Haru, Mako!

00:30:04.230 --> 00:30:05.290
You guys are late!

00:30:05.290 --> 00:30:08.620
Yeah, Haru and I joined the swim club.

00:30:08.620 --> 00:30:09.780
Swim club?

00:30:10.240 --> 00:30:13.220
At our school, everyone's required to join a club.

00:30:13.220 --> 00:30:14.290
Oh?

00:30:15.530 --> 00:30:17.540
We'll still try to come here when we can.

00:30:19.430 --> 00:30:21.420
Yeah, you've gotta!

00:30:21.420 --> 00:30:24.880
Oh, that reminds me.

00:30:24.880 --> 00:30:30.120
Coach said earlier that I'd swim breaststroke in the 50m and 100m races at the next meet!

00:30:30.120 --> 00:30:31.900
Really? That's great, Nagisa!

00:30:31.900 --> 00:30:32.430
Yeah!

00:30:32.760 --> 00:30:34.870
What about you two?

00:30:34.870 --> 00:30:41.480
Well, they said there'd be an official meet with the swim club, so I'll probably prioritize that.

00:30:41.480 --> 00:30:42.720
Really?

00:30:42.720 --> 00:30:44.250
What about you, Haru?

00:30:44.250 --> 00:30:46.090
I won't enter, either.

00:30:46.090 --> 00:30:47.510
I see...

00:30:50.600 --> 00:30:51.950
I'll go cheer for you, though.

00:30:51.950 --> 00:30:54.990
Yeah, we couldn't miss out on your spectacular swimming.

00:30:54.990 --> 00:30:55.920
Really?

00:30:55.920 --> 00:30:57.020
All right!

00:30:57.020 --> 00:30:58.460
I'll do my best!

00:30:58.460 --> 00:31:01.610
Nagisa! I told you not to run by the pool!

00:31:01.610 --> 00:31:03.210
S-Sorry!

00:31:07.720 --> 00:31:09.010
Sports

00:31:12.050 --> 00:31:14.060
Mental... Mental...

00:31:14.340 --> 00:31:16.380
Why are there so many?

00:31:16.380 --> 00:31:19.340
I have no idea which one of these I should get!

00:31:19.340 --> 00:31:21.810
Please keep it down.

00:31:22.100 --> 00:31:23.640
Sorry.

00:31:28.950 --> 00:31:30.650
Hey, do you like reading?!

00:31:30.650 --> 00:31:31.400
Hey!

00:31:31.400 --> 00:31:33.420
Your voice is too loud.

00:31:33.420 --> 00:31:36.330
What's with that sudden question?

00:31:36.330 --> 00:31:39.760
You're wearing glasses, so I figured you like reading.

00:31:39.760 --> 00:31:41.720
You're jumping to conclusions.

00:31:41.720 --> 00:31:43.980
Come on, please?

00:31:43.980 --> 00:31:47.950
I don't know which one to choose, and I'm in a tight spot.

00:31:53.830 --> 00:31:56.460
What kind of book are you looking for?

00:31:56.460 --> 00:31:58.940
I might be able to help you a little.

00:31:58.940 --> 00:31:59.430
Really?

00:31:59.910 --> 00:32:02.000
I want to be able to swim!

00:32:02.000 --> 00:32:03.860
I need a book to help me do that!

00:32:04.330 --> 00:32:06.820
If there's a book like that, then <i>I</i> want one!

00:32:06.820 --> 00:32:07.570
Huh? What'd you say?

00:32:07.940 --> 00:32:09.700
Nothing.

00:32:09.700 --> 00:32:12.360
Anyway, do you call that an explanation?

00:32:12.360 --> 00:32:14.480
You need to give more details.

00:32:14.480 --> 00:32:15.320
Oh, right.

00:32:15.700 --> 00:32:16.730
Let's see...

00:32:16.730 --> 00:32:21.240
I could swim the front crawl until yesterday, but then suddenly, I couldn't do it anymore.

00:32:22.180 --> 00:32:23.830
Does stuff like that happen?

00:32:24.180 --> 00:32:25.480
It did happen!

00:32:25.480 --> 00:32:27.070
I'm not lying!

00:32:27.070 --> 00:32:29.080
No, it can't be...

00:32:29.080 --> 00:32:30.640
But it's conceivable.

00:32:30.640 --> 00:32:32.840
If his mental state is affecting his body, then...

00:32:32.840 --> 00:32:34.590
What are you muttering about?

00:32:34.590 --> 00:32:36.810
I'm trying to help you here.

00:32:40.850 --> 00:32:43.770
Mental Training

00:32:40.850 --> 00:32:43.770
How to Maintain an
Unbreakable Spirit

00:32:41.150 --> 00:32:43.770
Why don't you try reading these?

00:32:43.770 --> 00:32:44.940
Thanks!

00:32:48.640 --> 00:32:51.070
Mental training books are great and all,

00:32:51.070 --> 00:32:54.590
but I think you should start by carefully self-reflecting.

00:32:54.590 --> 00:32:56.280
Really, thanks! You're a lifesaver!

00:32:56.280 --> 00:32:58.620
Hey! Listen until I'm done—

00:33:03.860 --> 00:33:05.880
Huh? What? What's going on?

00:33:05.880 --> 00:33:06.670
Hey, kid!

00:33:06.670 --> 00:33:08.620
You didn't check those out, did you?

00:33:08.620 --> 00:33:09.380
Check what out?

00:33:09.380 --> 00:33:11.210
You're coming with me.

00:33:10.040 --> 00:33:12.470
Hey! Huh? Wait—

00:33:14.700 --> 00:33:20.390
Genius... I'm a genius... I'm a genius... I'm a genius...

00:33:20.390 --> 00:33:24.570
I'm a genius. I'm a genius. I'm a genius.

00:33:20.390 --> 00:33:23.390
Mental Training

00:33:20.390 --> 00:33:23.390
How to Maintain an
Unbreakable Spirit\h\h

00:33:24.570 --> 00:33:28.140
I'm a genius! I'm a genius! I'm a genius!

00:33:28.140 --> 00:33:31.810
I... am a genius!

00:33:31.810 --> 00:33:33.690
Shut the hell up, Asahi!

00:33:39.880 --> 00:33:42.670
Man, basketball practice is tough.

00:33:42.670 --> 00:33:44.040
How's the swim club?

00:33:44.040 --> 00:33:45.050
Normal.

00:33:45.050 --> 00:33:47.270
That's your answer for everything, Haru.

00:33:51.360 --> 00:33:52.440
Kirishima.

00:33:52.440 --> 00:33:53.510
Wh-What?

00:33:54.110 --> 00:33:55.840
You want to eat with us too?

00:33:57.590 --> 00:33:58.960
I don't really...

00:34:04.090 --> 00:34:04.640
What?

00:34:06.280 --> 00:34:06.980
Nothing.

00:34:08.310 --> 00:34:09.440
Come on, eat with us.

00:34:10.020 --> 00:34:12.780
I want to talk to you too.

00:34:16.590 --> 00:34:18.750
I-I guess I don't have choice.

00:34:23.340 --> 00:34:24.830
I wouldn't want to be rude.

00:34:24.830 --> 00:34:26.860
Food! Food!

00:34:26.860 --> 00:34:27.960
Hey!

00:34:27.960 --> 00:34:30.420
Why are you sitting there?!

00:34:30.820 --> 00:34:33.160
I can sit wherever I want, can't I?

00:34:33.160 --> 00:34:35.660
That seat's reserved for me!

00:34:35.660 --> 00:34:38.020
Asahi, come sit here.

00:34:38.020 --> 00:34:40.450
Are you stupid?! Why?! No way!

00:34:40.450 --> 00:34:42.140
You're so funny.

00:34:44.550 --> 00:34:45.890
This sucks.

00:34:48.070 --> 00:34:50.760
You're actually a good guy, aren't you?

00:34:50.760 --> 00:34:52.630
Can it.

00:34:52.630 --> 00:34:54.430
Did the thing from yesterday get better?

00:34:54.430 --> 00:34:55.540
Oh, that?

00:34:55.540 --> 00:34:56.640
I dunno.

00:34:56.640 --> 00:34:58.450
Huh? Did something happen?

00:34:58.450 --> 00:35:00.890
This guy forgot how to swim.

00:35:00.890 --> 00:35:03.200
Just freestyle! Just that!

00:35:03.200 --> 00:35:04.540
Is that possible?

00:35:04.540 --> 00:35:05.700
Yeah, it is!

00:35:06.070 --> 00:35:09.600
But I borrowed books on mental training yesterday.

00:35:10.460 --> 00:35:12.640
So I'll be back to normal in no time!

00:35:15.240 --> 00:35:17.880
At least, I hope I will be.

00:35:20.310 --> 00:35:21.760
I'm stumped.

00:35:21.760 --> 00:35:22.700
Why?

00:35:22.700 --> 00:35:30.600
Well, step one of the first phase says to find your weaknesses...

00:35:31.820 --> 00:35:33.770
But since I'm perfect...

00:35:34.650 --> 00:35:36.840
I don't have any.

00:35:37.500 --> 00:35:39.490
So I'm stumped.

00:35:39.930 --> 00:35:42.200
I think your weakness is that you're stupid.

00:35:42.560 --> 00:35:43.280
Yeah, you're stupid.

00:35:43.620 --> 00:35:45.440
Asahi, you're so stupid!

00:35:46.500 --> 00:35:48.790
I'm gonna beat the crap outta you guys!

00:35:49.440 --> 00:35:52.100
That's what's so great about you.

00:35:52.100 --> 00:35:53.680
That doesn't make me happy!

00:35:55.540 --> 00:36:00.360
Anyway, the book said to talk about yourself positively.

00:36:00.360 --> 00:36:02.510
In other words, self-suggestion!

00:36:02.510 --> 00:36:07.360
That's why I thought I'd keep telling myself, "I'm a genius!" in the mirror!

00:36:08.480 --> 00:36:10.900
Is that really training?

00:36:10.900 --> 00:36:12.110
Yeah, isn't it?

00:36:12.110 --> 00:36:13.330
You really are stupid.

00:36:13.330 --> 00:36:14.360
What's wrong with you?

00:36:14.640 --> 00:36:16.650
You've sure been getting on my nerves...

00:36:16.650 --> 00:36:17.970
Isn't it fine?

00:36:17.970 --> 00:36:19.280
Right?

00:36:19.630 --> 00:36:22.830
It's how you look at things that matters, right?

00:36:22.830 --> 00:36:24.710
Yeah!

00:36:36.440 --> 00:36:37.090
What is it?

00:36:37.460 --> 00:36:38.000
What?

00:37:00.240 --> 00:37:01.820
What've you guys been doing?

00:37:02.420 --> 00:37:03.610
What is it, Ikuya?

00:37:03.610 --> 00:37:04.780
What are you talking about?!

00:37:05.320 --> 00:37:06.700
Don't copy me.

00:37:06.700 --> 00:37:08.080
I'm not!

00:37:09.840 --> 00:37:11.960
Ikuya, you're funny too!

00:37:11.960 --> 00:37:14.110
Hey! Don't lump me in with him!

00:37:14.110 --> 00:37:15.460
What do you mean by that?!

00:37:15.460 --> 00:37:17.050
Did I stutter?!

00:37:17.050 --> 00:37:20.000
Anyway, don't call me by my first name so naturally!

00:37:20.960 --> 00:37:23.200
Tachibana, make sure you wait!

00:37:23.200 --> 00:37:25.400
Yeah, I'm waiting.

00:37:27.780 --> 00:37:30.660
Haru, you're having fun with these guys too, aren't you?

00:37:30.660 --> 00:37:31.470
Not really.

00:37:31.470 --> 00:37:33.090
This isn't fun.

00:37:33.090 --> 00:37:35.970
I go out of my way to eat lunch with you and this is how I get treated?

00:37:35.970 --> 00:37:37.560
Go somewhere else, then!

00:37:37.560 --> 00:37:39.440
I can eat wherever I want, can't I?

00:37:39.440 --> 00:37:40.890
What's with that tone of voice?

00:37:40.890 --> 00:37:43.850
You're eating here 'cause you wanna copy Haru, right?

00:37:43.850 --> 00:37:45.490
I-I wasn't copying him!

00:37:45.490 --> 00:37:48.060
We just happened to be eating the same way!

00:37:50.260 --> 00:37:51.890
Is something the matter, Haru?

00:37:51.890 --> 00:37:52.960
It's nothing.

00:37:54.900 --> 00:37:58.840
Hey, who's the boy on class duty for Class 1?

00:37:58.840 --> 00:38:00.750
Wasn't it you today, Haru?

00:38:13.850 --> 00:38:15.690
That was close.

00:38:17.720 --> 00:38:18.850
How's club going?

00:38:19.660 --> 00:38:20.400
Normal...

00:38:20.720 --> 00:38:21.580
sir.

00:38:21.580 --> 00:38:23.250
I'm glad to hear that.

00:38:23.250 --> 00:38:25.920
I don't know what I would've done if you said you wanted to quit already.

00:38:26.820 --> 00:38:30.090
Has Ikuya... said anything about maybe wanting to quit?

00:38:33.000 --> 00:38:34.270
No, he hasn't.

00:38:34.270 --> 00:38:36.320
But maybe you should ask him yourself...

00:38:36.940 --> 00:38:38.080
sir.

00:38:38.080 --> 00:38:40.860
You have to work on speaking politely.

00:38:40.860 --> 00:38:42.190
You'll need to be able to in the future.

00:38:47.190 --> 00:38:49.260
Why don't you and Ikuya get along, sir?

00:38:54.550 --> 00:38:57.140
Probably because I pushed him away.

00:38:59.270 --> 00:39:03.250
That's why Ikuya's hated me for the past two years.

00:39:06.990 --> 00:39:08.280
I don't think that's true.

00:39:12.550 --> 00:39:13.780
I wonder.

00:39:15.130 --> 00:39:15.540
Here.

00:39:16.430 --> 00:39:17.440
Will you be okay?

00:39:17.440 --> 00:39:18.250
Don't drop them.

00:39:18.680 --> 00:39:22.670
Well, he's got some issues,
but I hope you can stay friends.

00:39:22.670 --> 00:39:24.880
See you at practice.

00:39:29.900 --> 00:39:31.340
Thank you very much.

00:39:35.360 --> 00:39:36.210
Sure!

00:39:36.210 --> 00:39:37.100
See ya!

00:39:49.930 --> 00:39:51.140
Hey, Ikuya.

00:39:51.140 --> 00:39:52.210
What's the matter?

00:39:52.210 --> 00:39:53.170
With what?

00:39:54.020 --> 00:39:54.770
Why are you copying—

00:39:54.770 --> 00:39:55.660
I'm not copying him!

00:39:56.990 --> 00:39:59.500
Do you know what's up with Ikuya?

00:39:59.500 --> 00:40:00.400
How should I know?

00:40:01.320 --> 00:40:02.530
Hey, first-years!

00:40:02.530 --> 00:40:04.400
Sir! Hello!

00:40:04.400 --> 00:40:05.280
Sir!

00:40:05.280 --> 00:40:05.660
Hey.

00:40:05.660 --> 00:40:06.310
Right.

00:40:09.030 --> 00:40:10.340
Ikuya, your greeting?

00:40:12.080 --> 00:40:12.590
Hey.

00:40:14.310 --> 00:40:15.350
How's it going, Asahi?

00:40:15.680 --> 00:40:17.230
Do you think you can swim freestyle?

00:40:17.230 --> 00:40:18.130
Yes!

00:40:18.130 --> 00:40:21.810
Nao said something about how it could be a mental issue,

00:40:21.810 --> 00:40:26.340
so I went to the library yesterday and
borrowed books about mental training!

00:40:26.340 --> 00:40:28.320
Really? Good job.

00:40:29.150 --> 00:40:30.300
I hope you'll be able to swim!

00:40:30.300 --> 00:40:31.130
Thank you, sir.

00:40:31.130 --> 00:40:32.400
So anyway, I'll be fine!

00:40:32.740 --> 00:40:33.590
I see.

00:40:34.860 --> 00:40:36.970
I'll leave the first-years to you, then.

00:40:36.970 --> 00:40:37.990
Right.

00:40:40.330 --> 00:40:42.120
Captain, shall we begin?

00:40:42.120 --> 00:40:43.600
Yeah, I'll be right there!

00:40:46.880 --> 00:40:48.840
He really is awkward.

00:40:54.240 --> 00:40:55.890
Well, shall we start?

00:40:55.890 --> 00:40:56.530
Yessir!

00:40:56.530 --> 00:40:56.990
Yes, sir!

00:40:56.990 --> 00:40:58.180
Yes, sir.

00:40:59.390 --> 00:41:01.140
We'll practice starting first.

00:41:02.040 --> 00:41:04.060
Let's try the track start.

00:41:04.560 --> 00:41:06.360
It's the one with one foot forward and one foot back.

00:41:09.530 --> 00:41:11.100
Don't bend your knees too much!

00:41:11.100 --> 00:41:13.120
Pay attention to your reaction time!

00:41:13.120 --> 00:41:14.000
Ready...

00:41:15.660 --> 00:41:16.620
Next!

00:41:21.080 --> 00:41:21.900
Ready...

00:41:30.630 --> 00:41:31.630
It's not good.

00:41:32.300 --> 00:41:35.380
There's too much time between the sound of the whistle and when you jump.

00:41:35.740 --> 00:41:39.140
You're not taking full advantage of the starting blocks.

00:41:39.140 --> 00:41:43.350
Try crouching with your focus under your belly button, around here.

00:41:44.100 --> 00:41:45.540
Everyone try it.

00:41:45.540 --> 00:41:47.940
That's where your body's center is located.

00:41:47.940 --> 00:41:48.850
How does it feel?

00:41:48.850 --> 00:41:50.370
It feels more stable, doesn't it?

00:41:51.260 --> 00:41:53.350
You'll feel more stable mentally too.

00:41:53.350 --> 00:41:57.520
Take a deep breath in that position and let it all out at once.

00:41:57.520 --> 00:42:00.550
It should feel like you let out all of your tension.

00:42:03.450 --> 00:42:05.540
The next part's important.

00:42:05.540 --> 00:42:09.040
After you exhale, take shallow breaths

00:42:09.820 --> 00:42:11.500
and imagine your whole body is ears.

00:42:11.910 --> 00:42:12.460
Ears?

00:42:12.460 --> 00:42:13.640
Yep.

00:42:13.640 --> 00:42:14.960
Ears.

00:42:14.960 --> 00:42:17.930
Like all the nerves in your body are
listening for the sound of the whistle.

00:42:18.210 --> 00:42:19.470
This is hard.

00:42:19.960 --> 00:42:20.760
Ears.

00:42:21.230 --> 00:42:23.450
It's hard to understand, right?

00:42:23.450 --> 00:42:24.400
That's fine.

00:42:24.400 --> 00:42:25.960
Huh? It is?

00:42:25.960 --> 00:42:26.770
Yeah.

00:42:26.770 --> 00:42:29.460
In the end, you just have to remember how it feels.

00:42:29.460 --> 00:42:30.960
Okay, guys. Come with me.

00:42:30.960 --> 00:42:31.570
Huh?

00:42:33.560 --> 00:42:34.990
Let's play a speed game.

00:42:35.440 --> 00:42:36.610
What?

00:42:39.400 --> 00:42:41.910
What is this?

00:42:42.670 --> 00:42:44.620
I told you, it's a speed game.

00:42:45.320 --> 00:42:48.770
Put both hands on the mat and lift your hips a little.

00:42:48.770 --> 00:42:52.250
And then, whoever grabs or swipes this cap first wins.

00:42:53.000 --> 00:42:57.220
If you keep practicing this, you'll develop a feel for what it means to turn your whole body into ears.

00:42:57.220 --> 00:42:58.730
I see...

00:42:58.730 --> 00:43:00.340
Okay, let's start with Haruka.

00:43:00.340 --> 00:43:01.770
Makoto, you'll blow the whistle.

00:43:01.770 --> 00:43:03.060
Yes, sir.

00:43:23.150 --> 00:43:24.330
Looks like I won.

00:43:29.750 --> 00:43:32.270
Haru's the slowest of us all!

00:43:32.270 --> 00:43:34.340
It's my turn next!

00:43:44.720 --> 00:43:45.680
You monster.

00:43:46.410 --> 00:43:47.350
Nothing, sir.

00:43:47.830 --> 00:43:50.100
Why is he a manager?

00:43:54.080 --> 00:43:57.150
Okay, next let's practice the relay exchange.

00:43:57.630 --> 00:44:00.840
We don't have much time before our practice swim meet with Sano Middle School.

00:44:01.540 --> 00:44:03.700
Haru, are you all right?

00:44:04.440 --> 00:44:05.450
I'm fine.

00:44:09.340 --> 00:44:11.000
Okay, get ready!

00:44:11.560 --> 00:44:12.650
On your marks.

00:44:16.560 --> 00:44:17.320
Get set.

00:44:35.560 --> 00:44:36.700
Ikuya, you were too fast!

00:44:36.700 --> 00:44:37.610
That was a false start!

00:44:49.490 --> 00:44:50.530
Too slow!

00:44:50.530 --> 00:44:52.410
That was slower than a standing start!

00:45:20.980 --> 00:45:22.320
Haruka, you're late too!

00:45:24.520 --> 00:45:25.320
Haru?

00:45:28.120 --> 00:45:29.830
His swimming's gotten sloppy.

00:45:30.240 --> 00:45:31.890
He swam fine yesterday.

00:45:46.670 --> 00:45:51.010
Why is he falling apart practicing for the relay?

00:45:54.460 --> 00:45:55.550
That's because...

00:45:56.810 --> 00:45:57.650
We...

00:45:59.380 --> 00:46:02.860
We won the medley relay in elementary school.

00:46:03.570 --> 00:46:06.480
That really was the best team ever,

00:46:08.860 --> 00:46:13.700
so Haru's probably having a hard time believing we can form a team better than that.

00:46:15.420 --> 00:46:16.540
I see.

00:46:17.820 --> 00:46:19.210
You're okay, though?

00:46:19.750 --> 00:46:21.720
I'm sad too, sir.

00:46:21.720 --> 00:46:24.090
But at least Haru is swimming with me.

00:46:24.400 --> 00:46:25.150
I see.

00:46:26.980 --> 00:46:28.300
Do you like swimming, Makoto?

00:46:29.320 --> 00:46:29.890
Yes.

00:46:30.940 --> 00:46:31.820
Really?

00:46:33.510 --> 00:46:35.020
It's not because Haruka is here?

00:46:45.080 --> 00:46:45.860
Sorry.

00:46:46.260 --> 00:46:48.130
That was a mean question.

00:46:49.310 --> 00:46:50.700
No, it's fine.

00:46:50.700 --> 00:46:52.330
Haru, you're almost there!

00:47:02.840 --> 00:47:03.660
Haru!

00:47:05.550 --> 00:47:06.670
Good job.

00:47:12.560 --> 00:47:13.600
Oh, Haru.

00:47:14.180 --> 00:47:15.180
Good job!

00:47:20.680 --> 00:47:24.360
In a relay, you can reduce your time a lot by improving your exchanges.

00:47:24.870 --> 00:47:28.740
But right now, I'm sure you're all faster as individuals.

00:47:36.620 --> 00:47:38.040
Okay, that's it for today!

00:47:38.400 --> 00:47:40.130
Go join the rest of the team and say bye!

00:47:40.130 --> 00:47:40.810
Yes, sir!

00:47:40.810 --> 00:47:41.590
Yes, sir.

00:47:42.350 --> 00:47:43.130
Yes, sir!

00:47:49.530 --> 00:47:50.800
Oh well.

00:47:51.310 --> 00:47:53.390
I'm sure it'll work out somehow.

00:47:54.630 --> 00:47:56.880
We don't have to be good at exchanges.

00:47:56.880 --> 00:47:59.520
As long as our individual times are fast,
it's not a problem.

00:48:00.740 --> 00:48:01.550
Makoto.

00:48:03.740 --> 00:48:04.600
Makoto.

00:48:06.110 --> 00:48:08.890
Oh, sorry, Haru. What is it?

00:48:08.890 --> 00:48:10.380
Did something happen?

00:48:10.380 --> 00:48:12.280
Huh? No, nothing.

00:48:12.280 --> 00:48:13.620
What, Makoto?

00:48:13.620 --> 00:48:15.370
You worried about the relay?

00:48:15.650 --> 00:48:18.250
Huh? Oh, yeah, I am.

00:48:18.250 --> 00:48:22.030
Like I said, it'll be fine! And we still have tons of time until the practice meet!

00:48:22.030 --> 00:48:24.130
Yeah, you're right.

00:48:24.660 --> 00:48:27.380
Okay, Ikuya and I are this way.

00:48:27.840 --> 00:48:30.500
How did we end up walking home together?

00:48:30.500 --> 00:48:33.010
Because we live in the same direction, of course.

00:48:33.800 --> 00:48:35.120
Hasty idiot.

00:48:35.120 --> 00:48:36.020
What did you say?!

00:48:36.020 --> 00:48:38.680
It's not like I said anything weird!

00:49:03.260 --> 00:49:04.090
Makoto.

00:49:05.060 --> 00:49:05.960
What is it?

00:49:08.760 --> 00:49:09.770
What happened?

00:49:13.130 --> 00:49:14.510
I said it was nothing.

00:49:14.790 --> 00:49:15.720
Don't lie to me!

00:49:19.050 --> 00:49:20.720
I'm not.

00:49:22.120 --> 00:49:22.960
Makoto?

00:49:22.960 --> 00:49:24.730
Really, it's nothing.

00:49:25.280 --> 00:49:27.060
Anyway, I'll see you tomorrow.

00:49:35.960 --> 00:49:36.860
I'm home.

00:49:38.000 --> 00:49:40.030
Oh, Haruka. Welcome back.

00:49:41.040 --> 00:49:44.000
There was a call from Dad's work today.

00:49:44.600 --> 00:49:47.130
They said he had been injured while he was working.

00:49:48.420 --> 00:49:49.180
And?

00:49:49.180 --> 00:49:51.780
Oh, it's not that bad.

00:49:51.780 --> 00:49:55.220
It just sounds like it'll be hard for him to get around until his injury heals,

00:49:55.900 --> 00:49:58.410
so I thought I'd go help him.

00:49:58.410 --> 00:49:59.740
How long will you be gone?

00:50:01.590 --> 00:50:03.730
Maybe about a week?

00:50:03.730 --> 00:50:05.420
What do you want to do?

00:50:05.420 --> 00:50:07.390
You still have school.

00:50:07.390 --> 00:50:09.480
I'm fine by myself for that long.

00:50:09.480 --> 00:50:10.860
Really?

00:50:10.860 --> 00:50:12.360
I'm worried, though.

00:50:13.050 --> 00:50:15.730
Well, I'll just ask the Tachibanas to keep an eye on you.

00:50:15.730 --> 00:50:16.450
'Kay.

00:50:42.920 --> 00:50:44.020
Really?

00:50:44.620 --> 00:50:46.270
It's not because Haruka is here?

00:50:50.550 --> 00:50:51.650
That's not it.

00:51:06.120 --> 00:51:08.620
Tachibana

00:51:06.720 --> 00:51:08.620
Oh, Haru. Good morning.

00:51:09.100 --> 00:51:12.630
Makoto said he had class duty and left early this morning.

00:51:13.950 --> 00:51:17.010
Oh, your mom's already with your dad, right?

00:51:17.770 --> 00:51:20.270
Come over for dinner starting tonight, okay?

00:51:20.270 --> 00:51:21.870
I'd be glad to.

00:51:48.880 --> 00:51:50.830
Hey, Makoto!

00:51:51.280 --> 00:51:53.160
Don't you have class duty today?

00:51:55.840 --> 00:51:57.050
What's wrong?

00:51:57.050 --> 00:51:59.720
Why did you want to swim so early in the morning?

00:52:00.310 --> 00:52:01.640
I mean...

00:52:02.390 --> 00:52:04.100
I just love swimming.

00:52:04.100 --> 00:52:05.370
What?

00:52:05.370 --> 00:52:07.060
Well, I'm off to school.

00:52:07.060 --> 00:52:08.180
R-Right.

00:52:09.880 --> 00:52:11.940
What's up with him?

00:52:12.810 --> 00:52:15.610
Huh? Haru, is that all you have for lunch?

00:52:16.010 --> 00:52:17.400
Grilled mackerel.

00:52:17.400 --> 00:52:19.320
It seems bland compared to yesterday.

00:52:20.190 --> 00:52:21.820
My parents won't be home for a while.

00:52:21.820 --> 00:52:24.600
What? How long's "a while"?

00:52:25.220 --> 00:52:26.210
About a week.

00:52:26.210 --> 00:52:29.260
What? Don't tell me you'll be by yourself that whole time?

00:52:29.260 --> 00:52:31.080
It's not a big deal.

00:52:31.080 --> 00:52:32.100
Really?

00:52:32.100 --> 00:52:33.750
There's no way I could do it.

00:52:35.000 --> 00:52:36.430
Me neither!

00:52:36.430 --> 00:52:38.180
Haru's fine even by himself...

00:52:38.180 --> 00:52:40.840
I'd die of starvation in three days.

00:52:41.520 --> 00:52:44.120
I bet you could live longer than three days without eating.

00:52:44.820 --> 00:52:45.860
Is that a compliment?

00:52:45.860 --> 00:52:47.350
Of course!

00:52:45.860 --> 00:52:46.700
It's bitter.

00:52:50.350 --> 00:52:53.730
Okay, next is five intervals of 50m freestyle.

00:52:55.080 --> 00:52:56.110
Asahi, can you do it?

00:52:56.110 --> 00:52:57.230
Y-Yes, sir!

00:52:59.190 --> 00:53:00.760
I'll be timing you too.

00:53:00.760 --> 00:53:02.150
Haruka, you first.

00:53:22.710 --> 00:53:23.930
Next, Asahi.

00:53:23.930 --> 00:53:25.530
Y-Yes, sir!

00:53:46.610 --> 00:53:47.820
Damn it.

00:53:48.260 --> 00:53:50.280
Asahi, you don't have to push yourself!

00:53:50.280 --> 00:53:51.700
Damn it!

00:53:52.010 --> 00:53:53.020
Next, Makoto.

00:53:53.020 --> 00:53:54.290
Y-Yes, sir!

00:53:59.380 --> 00:54:00.300
Hey, Haru.

00:54:01.460 --> 00:54:03.660
How do you swim freestyle?

00:54:04.410 --> 00:54:08.290
I thrust my fingers into the water's surface without fighting against it to make a cut,

00:54:08.290 --> 00:54:10.290
then slide my body in after.

00:54:10.920 --> 00:54:12.390
What does that even mean?!

00:54:13.710 --> 00:54:15.190
I used to be able to swim it...

00:54:18.820 --> 00:54:20.230
Okay, swim your specialties next.

00:54:21.140 --> 00:54:23.700
Do five 100m intervals, one every three minutes.

00:54:23.700 --> 00:54:25.330
I'll be timing these too.

00:54:32.240 --> 00:54:33.200
Let's race.

00:54:46.490 --> 00:54:47.550
Jeez, those two...

00:54:54.710 --> 00:54:55.600
Who won?

00:54:55.960 --> 00:54:57.370
You did by a hair.

00:54:57.370 --> 00:54:58.440
All right!

00:55:08.020 --> 00:55:08.660
Makoto?

00:55:08.660 --> 00:55:11.820
Makoto, didn't you swim more than ten lengths?

00:55:12.490 --> 00:55:13.980
I did an extra one...

00:55:15.950 --> 00:55:19.040
It won't help you get better if you swim recklessly, you know.

00:55:19.040 --> 00:55:20.080
I'm fine...

00:55:20.470 --> 00:55:23.120
After I rest a little... I'll swim...

00:55:24.270 --> 00:55:25.550
another interval...

00:55:29.430 --> 00:55:30.500
How's it going?

00:55:30.500 --> 00:55:32.620
Their individual times aren't bad.

00:55:32.620 --> 00:55:35.190
The problem is their relay exchanges.

00:55:36.790 --> 00:55:38.270
We'll be practicing the relay from now on.

00:55:38.680 --> 00:55:39.270
Yes, sir.

00:55:42.250 --> 00:55:43.020
Ready.

00:55:50.630 --> 00:55:52.160
That was slow! You're being too careful!

00:55:55.700 --> 00:55:57.290
Too fast! Watch closely!

00:56:01.710 --> 00:56:03.280
Too slow! Are you even trying?

00:56:07.940 --> 00:56:09.000
You're slow.

00:56:09.910 --> 00:56:11.440
Why do you think that is?

00:56:12.070 --> 00:56:14.350
The exchanges... sir?

00:56:14.350 --> 00:56:15.570
That's right.

00:56:15.570 --> 00:56:18.150
So why aren't the exchanges going well?

00:56:19.740 --> 00:56:21.250
Do you want to swim the relay?

00:56:23.460 --> 00:56:25.150
We can just all swim in individual events.

00:56:27.470 --> 00:56:29.490
I'm fine with just the individual freestyle.

00:56:29.490 --> 00:56:30.280
Haru...

00:56:30.560 --> 00:56:31.390
I already told you!

00:56:31.390 --> 00:56:34.490
If you aren't in it, then they won't be able to compete in the relay!

00:56:35.220 --> 00:56:37.580
Everyone else also thinks we should race individually.

00:56:37.580 --> 00:56:38.720
That's true.

00:56:38.720 --> 00:56:41.340
In the first place, we can't do a relay with this team.

00:56:41.340 --> 00:56:42.820
Don't say that!

00:56:42.820 --> 00:56:44.920
I don't feel the same way!

00:56:45.380 --> 00:56:47.250
Then meet me halfway or something!

00:56:47.670 --> 00:56:50.430
Asahi, your swimming is too self-centered!

00:56:50.430 --> 00:56:51.590
Sh-Shut up!

00:56:51.590 --> 00:56:52.510
Stop it!

00:56:52.510 --> 00:56:56.970
Your exchanges aren't going well because you're all just thinking about yourselves!

00:56:58.720 --> 00:57:00.220
Individual events and relays are different!

00:57:00.830 --> 00:57:02.350
Think carefully about what that means!

00:57:03.070 --> 00:57:04.730
All of you, go cool your heads!

00:57:16.570 --> 00:57:17.510
Asahi!

00:57:20.250 --> 00:57:21.510
Nao.

00:57:22.160 --> 00:57:22.870
Hey.

00:57:24.120 --> 00:57:26.920
Natsuya was pretty harsh on you guys, huh?

00:57:27.620 --> 00:57:30.310
No, he was just telling the truth, sir.

00:57:33.520 --> 00:57:34.480
Nao.

00:57:36.340 --> 00:57:38.350
It's just as Ikuya said.

00:57:39.600 --> 00:57:43.550
I'm only thinking about myself when I'm swimming.

00:57:44.800 --> 00:57:46.400
That's what I think, sir.

00:57:48.120 --> 00:57:49.090
I see.

00:57:50.390 --> 00:57:51.340
I mean,

00:57:52.190 --> 00:57:54.120
I can't even think about the relay.

00:57:55.240 --> 00:57:56.170
I'm scared.

00:57:56.920 --> 00:57:57.910
What do you mean?

00:58:02.990 --> 00:58:04.010
Hey.

00:58:05.040 --> 00:58:05.920
What...

00:58:10.190 --> 00:58:11.010
What if...

00:58:12.800 --> 00:58:15.930
What if I stop being able to swim the other strokes too?!

00:58:39.690 --> 00:58:40.540
Makoto.

00:58:40.540 --> 00:58:41.870
Wh-What is it?

00:58:42.490 --> 00:58:45.460
You were practicing recklessly today, weren't you?

00:58:45.460 --> 00:58:47.230
That's not true.

00:58:47.230 --> 00:58:49.640
Your pace and number of laps were both higher than usual.

00:58:49.640 --> 00:58:52.630
I mean, we have a meet coming up.

00:58:52.920 --> 00:58:55.420
I just like swimming, that's all.

00:58:58.180 --> 00:58:59.960
Where did that come from?

00:59:00.980 --> 00:59:03.370
That reaction's mean, Haru.

00:59:03.370 --> 00:59:05.050
I just like it,

00:59:05.050 --> 00:59:08.390
and that makes me want to swim a lot more.

00:59:15.740 --> 00:59:16.320
Today...

00:59:17.980 --> 00:59:19.800
What is it?

00:59:19.800 --> 00:59:21.250
You go first.

00:59:22.100 --> 00:59:22.660
Okay.

00:59:24.640 --> 00:59:30.090
Today, during practice, why did you say
it was fine to just be in individual events?

00:59:30.090 --> 00:59:31.450
There was no real reason.

00:59:31.450 --> 00:59:33.310
I just said what I thought.

00:59:34.480 --> 00:59:36.540
I never liked relays to begin with.

00:59:36.540 --> 00:59:39.430
You swam them in elementary school.

00:59:40.000 --> 00:59:42.050
Things are different now.

00:59:42.050 --> 00:59:43.530
I don't feel like doing them anymore.

00:59:44.830 --> 00:59:48.610
Rin was the one who convinced you when you didn't want to do it, huh?

00:59:50.330 --> 00:59:52.460
Don't talk about someone who isn't here.

00:59:52.460 --> 00:59:54.560
You're right. Sorry.

00:59:55.780 --> 00:59:57.940
What were you about to say earlier?

01:00:00.750 --> 01:00:02.070
Why'd you leave without me this morning?

01:00:06.420 --> 01:00:09.100
I had class duty today, so, um...

01:00:10.080 --> 01:00:12.280
Sorry. I forgot to tell you.

01:00:12.280 --> 01:00:14.170
You've never forgotten to tell me before.

01:00:16.030 --> 01:00:18.300
Maybe I haven't, but...

01:00:19.300 --> 01:00:22.180
Getting used to all this new stuff is really hard!

01:00:22.180 --> 01:00:24.430
Didn't you say so yourself just now?!

01:00:25.080 --> 01:00:27.010
That it's different now?!

01:00:30.840 --> 01:00:32.040
That's true.

01:00:47.470 --> 01:00:49.750
Haru, you're coming over for dinner, right?

01:00:50.660 --> 01:00:52.000
I'll eat at home today.

01:00:52.000 --> 01:00:54.890
Huh? But your mom already left, didn't she?

01:00:54.890 --> 01:00:56.370
I'll figure something out on my own.

01:00:59.080 --> 01:01:00.170
Thanks for the food.

01:01:08.810 --> 01:01:11.060
I'm a genius. I'm a genius.

01:01:11.060 --> 01:01:12.310
I'm a genius...

01:01:12.700 --> 01:01:14.650
I am... a genius...

01:01:23.600 --> 01:01:25.420
Why not change up our training?

01:01:25.420 --> 01:01:26.490
What are you talking about?

01:01:32.110 --> 01:01:34.510
Even if we don't practice exchanges,

01:01:34.510 --> 01:01:36.820
if we can do our personal bests, then the relay—

01:01:36.820 --> 01:01:39.960
That attitude is why it's hard for you to sync with the other guys.

01:01:40.790 --> 01:01:42.750
Are you saying it's my fault?!

01:01:42.750 --> 01:01:45.050
The rest of the guys are all thinking the same thing!

01:01:45.050 --> 01:01:49.060
Don't insult your friends while
being blind to your own faults.

01:01:49.670 --> 01:01:51.440
A relay requires a team, doesn't it?

01:01:53.180 --> 01:01:54.130
A team?

01:01:54.890 --> 01:01:55.920
Friends?

01:01:57.110 --> 01:01:59.180
Are you one to talk?

01:02:00.490 --> 01:02:04.100
It's easy for you to tell me to expand
my horizons and make new friends...

01:02:05.430 --> 01:02:09.450
You were the first one to push me aside!

01:02:10.250 --> 01:02:11.290
Ikuya!

01:02:28.630 --> 01:02:32.140
I wish the captain wouldn't skip practice.

01:02:32.140 --> 01:02:33.430
Leave me alone.

01:02:34.390 --> 01:02:37.040
Why don't you stop pushing
him away on purpose already?

01:02:37.040 --> 01:02:38.980
Or do you like being depressed?

01:02:38.980 --> 01:02:40.820
How did you know?

01:02:41.220 --> 01:02:44.240
It's not hard to figure out what would make you depressed.

01:02:44.240 --> 01:02:45.910
Shut up.

01:02:45.910 --> 01:02:47.770
This is fine.

01:02:47.770 --> 01:02:51.010
If I don't do this, then he won't ever get out of my shadow.

01:02:53.430 --> 01:02:54.330
How's Asahi?

01:02:55.380 --> 01:02:56.490
He's scared.

01:02:57.110 --> 01:02:58.680
But I think he'll be fine.

01:02:59.340 --> 01:03:02.340
He's got an innate strength and desire to improve himself.

01:03:02.340 --> 01:03:03.350
I see.

01:03:03.350 --> 01:03:06.160
I bet he'll make a great captain one day.

01:03:07.300 --> 01:03:07.930
What about Makoto?

01:03:08.400 --> 01:03:09.510
He's wavering.

01:03:10.040 --> 01:03:13.460
But I think he'll be stronger once he breaks through.

01:03:14.530 --> 01:03:15.400
And Haruka?

01:03:15.810 --> 01:03:17.140
He's a prodigy.

01:03:17.140 --> 01:03:20.200
You rarely see such a clean streamline.

01:03:21.230 --> 01:03:24.590
But he starts falling apart when it comes to the relay.

01:03:24.590 --> 01:03:27.280
If only he could pay a little more attention to his surroundings...

01:03:28.340 --> 01:03:29.610
He's the same as Ikuya, huh?

01:03:32.090 --> 01:03:32.990
What about Ikuya?

01:03:33.490 --> 01:03:35.830
He swims in a way that minimizes fatigue.

01:03:36.590 --> 01:03:39.450
That's why his pace doesn't drop
even when he swims long distances.

01:03:42.490 --> 01:03:44.750
Isn't my little brother amazing?

01:03:45.380 --> 01:03:47.260
He'll get faster.

01:03:47.660 --> 01:03:48.840
I'm counting on you.

01:03:48.840 --> 01:03:49.480
Yeah.

01:04:46.640 --> 01:04:50.820
Now then, let's begin the practice swim meet between Sano Middle School and Iwatobi Middle School!

01:04:51.260 --> 01:04:52.490
Let's do our best!

01:04:53.490 --> 01:04:55.180
Nanase, Tachibana.

01:04:56.200 --> 01:04:56.950
Um...

01:04:57.240 --> 01:04:59.700
I'm Yamazaki Sousuke from Sano SC.

01:04:59.700 --> 01:05:01.440
Sano SC?

01:05:01.440 --> 01:05:02.770
The one Rin went to?

01:05:02.770 --> 01:05:03.330
That's right.

01:05:03.950 --> 01:05:06.540
Nanase, let's see who's faster at freestyle.

01:05:07.880 --> 01:05:08.730
Later.

01:05:13.370 --> 01:05:14.740
Ready...

01:05:15.770 --> 01:05:17.010
Go!

01:05:17.790 --> 01:05:21.260
Go, go, go, go, go, Makoto!

01:05:21.260 --> 01:05:27.190
Swim, swim, swim, swim, swim, Makoto!

01:05:28.600 --> 01:05:30.170
Good work!

01:05:32.900 --> 01:05:38.380
Go, go, go, go, go, Ikuya!

01:05:38.380 --> 01:05:39.490
Good work!

01:05:43.620 --> 01:05:49.970
Go, go, go, go, go, Asahi!

01:05:49.970 --> 01:05:51.670
Good work!

01:05:53.880 --> 01:06:00.180
Go, go, go, go, go, Haruka!

01:06:00.180 --> 01:06:06.270
Swim, swim, swim, swim, swim, Haruka!

01:06:06.270 --> 01:06:12.400
Go, go, go, go, go, Haruka!

01:06:12.400 --> 01:06:15.710
Swim, swim, swim, swim, swim, Haruka!

01:06:15.710 --> 01:06:17.150
Good work!

01:06:19.540 --> 01:06:20.910
Nanase!

01:06:20.910 --> 01:06:22.540
Are you underestimating me?!

01:06:22.540 --> 01:06:23.950
Stop that, Sousuke!

01:06:38.850 --> 01:06:39.970
Ready...

01:06:41.300 --> 01:06:42.390
Go!

01:06:42.780 --> 01:06:46.070
Go, go, go, go, go, Makoto!

01:06:55.320 --> 01:06:56.650
They're not even trying.

01:07:03.510 --> 01:07:04.450
Damn it!

01:07:05.750 --> 01:07:06.410
Slowpoke.

01:07:14.290 --> 01:07:15.710
Haru's so slow.

01:07:16.940 --> 01:07:20.160
Go, go, go, go, go, Haruka!

01:07:20.160 --> 01:07:23.410
Swim, swim, swim, swim, swim, Haruka!

01:07:23.410 --> 01:07:25.030
Good work!

01:07:28.910 --> 01:07:29.670
Haru.

01:07:32.560 --> 01:07:33.650
I'm fine.

01:07:44.360 --> 01:07:45.710
Good work, everyone.

01:07:45.710 --> 01:07:48.410
Take the rest of the day off.
We'll start at it again tomorrow.

01:07:48.410 --> 01:07:49.160
Yes, sir!

01:07:49.520 --> 01:07:50.760
Okay, that's all!

01:07:50.760 --> 01:07:52.750
Thank you very much!

01:07:54.890 --> 01:07:56.090
Hey, first-years.

01:07:56.860 --> 01:07:58.240
How was the relay?

01:07:59.820 --> 01:08:01.890
You guys will never beat Sano.

01:08:02.180 --> 01:08:03.500
Not like you are now.

01:08:04.160 --> 01:08:06.970
They're functioning much better as a team.

01:08:06.970 --> 01:08:08.210
He's right.

01:08:08.210 --> 01:08:10.180
You can't win if you don't change.

01:08:10.180 --> 01:08:12.370
You need to polish your teamwork by the official meet.

01:08:12.370 --> 01:08:15.580
Individually, you're all definitely better.

01:08:24.160 --> 01:08:25.870
Hey, Nanase Haruka!

01:08:26.230 --> 01:08:27.120
Yamazaki?

01:08:27.420 --> 01:08:28.880
What was with that swimming?

01:08:28.880 --> 01:08:30.360
Are you too good for me?

01:08:30.360 --> 01:08:32.370
This has nothing to do with you. Stop complaining.

01:08:32.370 --> 01:08:33.250
Stop messing around!

01:08:34.090 --> 01:08:35.530
What did you say?!

01:08:35.530 --> 01:08:36.140
It's fine.

01:08:36.140 --> 01:08:37.520
Huh? But...

01:08:37.520 --> 01:08:38.320
I said, it's fine.

01:08:39.720 --> 01:08:44.210
Have you ever thought about how
Rin must feel when he swims now?

01:08:44.210 --> 01:08:45.090
Rin?

01:08:46.130 --> 01:08:49.520
You think he'd be satisfied with that kind of swimming?!

01:08:49.520 --> 01:08:52.910
I'm not swimming to make Rin happy.

01:08:54.070 --> 01:08:54.900
C'mon, guys.

01:08:55.500 --> 01:08:57.140
Calm down a little.

01:08:58.030 --> 01:09:02.150
Don't forget Rin's desire to swim with you.

01:09:02.150 --> 01:09:05.120
If you swim half-heartedly, I won't forgive you!

01:09:08.490 --> 01:09:09.950
A letter from Rin...

01:09:09.950 --> 01:09:10.750
From Rin?

01:09:22.490 --> 01:09:23.590
You're not going to read it?

01:09:25.580 --> 01:09:26.440
No, I'm not.

01:09:41.850 --> 01:09:44.320
I'm going in April.

01:09:45.820 --> 01:09:48.490
I see. Finally leaving for Australia, huh?

01:09:48.490 --> 01:09:49.420
Yeah.

01:09:49.420 --> 01:09:52.650
I know your dad would be proud of you, aiming for the world stage like he did.

01:09:52.650 --> 01:09:54.380
Well, I don't know.

01:09:54.380 --> 01:09:54.870
Huh?

01:09:55.240 --> 01:09:59.460
But I feel like if I jump into somewhere foreign,
I can figure the rest out myself.

01:10:00.980 --> 01:10:02.420
That's just like you.

01:10:02.420 --> 01:10:05.430
Oh, I'll go to Iwatobi before that.

01:10:05.430 --> 01:10:06.800
To Iwatobi?

01:10:06.800 --> 01:10:08.190
Why?

01:10:08.190 --> 01:10:12.890
I found someone there I want to swim a relay with.

01:10:23.140 --> 01:10:24.280
At Iwatobi,

01:10:24.580 --> 01:10:27.190
Nanase swims freestyle, so you'll swim butterfly then?

01:10:27.190 --> 01:10:29.070
I guess so.

01:10:29.070 --> 01:10:31.160
Oh, Sousuke, can you swim butterfly?

01:10:31.530 --> 01:10:33.660
Better than you.

01:10:33.660 --> 01:10:36.170
What's that about? Trying to make me mad?

01:10:44.090 --> 01:10:47.170
Haru, come over for dinner tonight.

01:10:47.170 --> 01:10:47.590
I'm fine.

01:10:48.080 --> 01:10:49.070
I'll eat at home.

01:10:53.310 --> 01:10:54.540
Hey, dinner's ready.

01:10:54.540 --> 01:10:55.520
I'm not hungry!

01:10:59.080 --> 01:11:00.310
I'm a genius.

01:11:00.310 --> 01:11:02.450
I'm a genius. I'm a genius...

01:11:03.990 --> 01:11:07.200
Am I really a genius?

01:11:32.180 --> 01:11:33.110
Haru.

01:11:34.260 --> 01:11:35.720
Is that your dinner?

01:11:34.260 --> 01:11:35.720
Rice

01:11:34.260 --> 01:11:35.720
Mackerel

01:11:38.040 --> 01:11:39.350
What I eat isn't your business.

01:11:39.350 --> 01:11:41.130
Yes, it is!

01:11:41.130 --> 01:11:44.720
You haven't been eating the food
I've been bringing over, have you?

01:11:44.720 --> 01:11:46.490
No wonder you were low on stamina today!

01:11:47.070 --> 01:11:49.700
It's fine if you don't want to eat with me!

01:11:49.700 --> 01:11:51.320
But don't tell me you'll figure some—

01:11:50.680 --> 01:11:51.910
Be quiet!

01:11:52.810 --> 01:11:54.330
Everyone's acting selfishly!

01:11:54.830 --> 01:11:56.120
What about you?

01:11:56.460 --> 01:11:57.580
You've changed too!

01:11:57.580 --> 01:12:00.540
Meanwhile you tell me nothing's going on!

01:12:01.540 --> 01:12:03.630
What are you doing?

01:12:04.250 --> 01:12:08.220
Why are you trying to force yourself to become something you're not?

01:12:10.340 --> 01:12:11.130
Haru.

01:12:13.690 --> 01:12:15.640
You should just be yourself.

01:12:36.360 --> 01:12:37.910
Be myself...

01:12:39.270 --> 01:12:40.030
Mako—

01:12:40.030 --> 01:12:40.830
Haru!

01:12:41.260 --> 01:12:42.690
Come with me!

01:12:43.600 --> 01:12:45.050
Let's go, Haru!

01:12:45.050 --> 01:12:45.890
H-Hey!

01:13:45.450 --> 01:13:47.020
This feels good.

01:13:54.150 --> 01:13:58.780
I thought I'd be different in middle school.

01:13:59.330 --> 01:14:00.990
I thought I wanted to change.

01:14:00.990 --> 01:14:05.250
But somehow, I ended up freaking out,
like I had to change.

01:14:06.500 --> 01:14:10.920
Nao asked me if it wasn't that I liked swimming,

01:14:10.920 --> 01:14:14.190
but that I was swimming because of you.

01:14:14.920 --> 01:14:15.970
I see.

01:14:18.290 --> 01:14:22.980
I'd never thought about it before,
and I couldn't tell if I liked swimming,

01:14:23.760 --> 01:14:26.950
or if I just wanted to be with you.

01:14:27.930 --> 01:14:29.480
Is that why you were avoiding me?

01:14:29.480 --> 01:14:32.220
I wasn't trying to avoid you, really.

01:14:32.220 --> 01:14:36.200
I just thought I'd have an even harder time figuring out how I felt if I was with you,

01:14:36.200 --> 01:14:37.950
so it was hard to be together.

01:14:39.100 --> 01:14:42.140
It just looked like I was avoiding you, huh?

01:14:43.700 --> 01:14:45.210
I'm sorry, Haru.

01:14:47.250 --> 01:14:48.360
It's fine.

01:14:48.360 --> 01:14:49.670
I was wrong too.

01:14:52.550 --> 01:14:55.140
So, did you find your answer?

01:14:55.140 --> 01:14:56.680
I think it's both.

01:14:56.680 --> 01:14:57.680
Both?

01:14:57.990 --> 01:14:58.660
Yeah.

01:14:59.410 --> 01:15:02.670
For a while, I lost confidence in my own feelings,

01:15:03.290 --> 01:15:05.600
and I forced myself to try too hard.

01:15:06.440 --> 01:15:07.360
But now,

01:15:08.210 --> 01:15:09.440
I'm really having fun.

01:15:09.960 --> 01:15:13.440
Just swimming like this feels so good.

01:15:15.580 --> 01:15:17.900
I really do like swimming.

01:15:19.630 --> 01:15:22.200
But I want you to be there too.

01:15:30.810 --> 01:15:36.210
I love swimming and you,
so I want to swim together, bro!

01:15:57.450 --> 01:15:59.370
I told you to stop calling me that.

01:15:59.370 --> 01:16:00.390
You did.

01:16:00.390 --> 01:16:01.150
Sorry.

01:16:01.920 --> 01:16:03.280
And...

01:16:03.770 --> 01:16:06.040
of course I'll swim with you.

01:16:08.850 --> 01:16:09.410
Right!

01:16:09.410 --> 01:16:10.640
Let's go home, Makoto.

01:16:10.640 --> 01:16:12.920
Oh, wait up, Haru!

01:16:20.080 --> 01:16:21.170
Nao.

01:16:22.780 --> 01:16:23.720
Makoto.

01:16:25.040 --> 01:16:26.100
What did you want to talk about?

01:16:27.040 --> 01:16:30.690
I really like Haru's swimming.

01:16:30.690 --> 01:16:34.110
I don't deny that I swam because Haru was there.

01:16:34.420 --> 01:16:38.510
But I was really frustrated when we lost the relay.

01:16:40.660 --> 01:16:41.110
Yeah.

01:16:41.500 --> 01:16:43.620
I like swimming.

01:16:44.370 --> 01:16:45.030
That's why...

01:16:45.660 --> 01:16:47.260
That's why I definitely...

01:16:48.710 --> 01:16:50.040
want to win the next relay!

01:16:51.520 --> 01:16:52.420
I see.

01:16:53.090 --> 01:16:54.580
I just wanted to say that.

01:16:56.300 --> 01:16:57.910
I'm sure you'll be able to win next time.

01:16:59.660 --> 01:17:00.380
Yes, sir!

01:17:04.820 --> 01:17:06.760
Guys, let's go to practice!

01:17:07.150 --> 01:17:07.880
Makoto?

01:17:07.880 --> 01:17:10.520
What's the matter? You don't usually come here.

01:17:10.520 --> 01:17:12.260
Oh, it's nothing much.

01:17:12.260 --> 01:17:14.030
Really? It's fine, anyway.

01:17:14.030 --> 01:17:15.110
Hey, Ikuya!

01:17:15.110 --> 01:17:16.300
We're going to practice!

01:17:17.360 --> 01:17:18.340
I'm not going.

01:17:19.230 --> 01:17:19.840
Ikuya?

01:17:19.840 --> 01:17:21.080
Don't be stupid!

01:17:21.080 --> 01:17:22.880
Let's practice for the relay!

01:17:22.880 --> 01:17:24.930
We're gonna get revenge on Sano Middle School!

01:17:27.260 --> 01:17:28.120
Not my problem.

01:17:29.250 --> 01:17:31.120
I'm quitting the swim club.

01:17:32.770 --> 01:17:34.000
What are you saying?!

01:17:34.350 --> 01:17:35.670
Stop joking around!

01:17:35.670 --> 01:17:36.250
Ikuya?

01:17:37.270 --> 01:17:39.080
That sorta joke isn't funny!

01:17:39.080 --> 01:17:39.980
You hear me?!

01:17:39.980 --> 01:17:40.710
Shut up!

01:17:41.420 --> 01:17:42.920
I'm quitting!

01:17:44.310 --> 01:17:45.140
Hey!

01:17:45.140 --> 01:17:46.140
Wait up, Ikuya!

01:17:46.140 --> 01:17:47.980
Hey, you two!

01:17:47.980 --> 01:17:49.640
C'mon, Haru!

01:17:49.640 --> 01:17:50.890
Again?

01:17:57.770 --> 01:17:58.940
Wait!

01:17:58.940 --> 01:18:00.670
Don't be so hasty!

01:18:03.810 --> 01:18:05.320
That hurts, dude!

01:18:05.320 --> 01:18:06.310
You idiot!

01:18:06.310 --> 01:18:07.320
Don't try to...

01:18:07.620 --> 01:18:09.960
Don't try to kill yourself just because you lost once!

01:18:10.580 --> 01:18:12.170
Like I would!

01:18:12.170 --> 01:18:13.940
I wasn't trying to kill myself!

01:18:13.940 --> 01:18:14.750
Jeez...

01:18:14.750 --> 01:18:16.450
Are you stupid?

01:18:16.450 --> 01:18:18.090
Get off me. I can't move.

01:18:23.320 --> 01:18:26.010
Why did you all come?

01:18:26.010 --> 01:18:28.780
Why wouldn't we?! We're worried about you!

01:18:30.880 --> 01:18:32.020
Why?

01:18:33.260 --> 01:18:35.350
Because we're a team.

01:18:40.480 --> 01:18:40.820
Huh?

01:18:40.820 --> 01:18:41.940
Bandou Swimming Club

01:18:41.560 --> 01:18:43.320
Wait, is that...

01:18:41.940 --> 01:18:43.690
Bandou Swimming Club

01:18:45.870 --> 01:18:48.460
It's the SC my brother and I used to go to.

01:18:49.420 --> 01:18:53.580
We said we wanted to compete internationally together,
and we worked hard for that goal.

01:18:53.580 --> 01:19:04.300
Bandou Swimming Club

01:18:54.500 --> 01:18:59.010
But the second he became a middle schooler,
he pushed me away.

01:18:59.010 --> 01:19:04.300
When I asked him why, he just told me to
expand my horizons and make new friends.

01:19:05.090 --> 01:19:07.430
I was getting in his way.

01:19:08.330 --> 01:19:11.300
I just couldn't forgive him for that.

01:19:11.630 --> 01:19:13.600
I don't think that's what he meant.

01:19:13.600 --> 01:19:17.940
I think he just wanted you to be able to do it on your own.

01:19:18.570 --> 01:19:22.820
As a big brother like him, I think it's a little sad, though.

01:19:25.030 --> 01:19:27.820
Natsuya is worried about you.

01:19:28.680 --> 01:19:30.730
He said it wasn't your fault if you hated him.

01:19:31.810 --> 01:19:33.250
He sounded lonely.

01:19:34.910 --> 01:19:40.750
There really isn't a big brother who hates his little brother, Ikuya.

01:19:41.450 --> 01:19:43.030
You're not alone.

01:19:45.570 --> 01:19:49.090
I always thought it was fine as long as he was there...

01:19:49.670 --> 01:19:51.270
As long as he was there,

01:19:52.690 --> 01:19:56.560
I didn't need teammates or friends...

01:19:57.890 --> 01:19:59.190
That's why...

01:19:59.190 --> 01:20:03.690
Bandou Swimming Club

01:19:59.890 --> 01:20:03.690
when he wasn't there anymore, I swam by myself.

01:20:04.490 --> 01:20:06.400
But actually, the whole time...

01:20:08.400 --> 01:20:09.930
I was really lonely.

01:20:10.870 --> 01:20:12.810
Lonely...

01:20:12.810 --> 01:20:14.530
I thought, if I could be like Haru,

01:20:15.170 --> 01:20:18.530
then maybe he would pay attention to me again.

01:20:18.530 --> 01:20:20.540
Is that why you were copying Haru?

01:20:21.860 --> 01:20:23.620
And you call me stupid?

01:20:23.620 --> 01:20:26.550
You're fast enough without having to do stuff like that.

01:20:27.050 --> 01:20:29.420
Natsuya knows that too.

01:20:31.880 --> 01:20:33.600
Right, Haru?

01:20:37.650 --> 01:20:40.850
Was I lonely too?

01:20:41.420 --> 01:20:42.600
Huh? Did you say something?

01:20:45.160 --> 01:20:46.070
Ikuya.

01:20:46.690 --> 01:20:48.070
You're not me.

01:20:48.660 --> 01:20:50.820
You don't belong in my shadow or Natsuya's either.

01:20:51.490 --> 01:20:53.000
Line up next to the rest of us.

01:21:07.270 --> 01:21:09.800
A-A towel! A towel, a towel!

01:21:09.800 --> 01:21:10.380
I don't have one?!

01:21:10.380 --> 01:21:12.470
All right, wipe with this!

01:21:14.920 --> 01:21:16.720
Why would I want to use something that dirty?

01:21:17.810 --> 01:21:19.550
Wh-What do you mean, dirty?!

01:21:19.550 --> 01:21:21.430
It's washed everyday—

01:21:31.460 --> 01:21:34.110
All right! Let's go back to practice!

01:21:34.990 --> 01:21:36.370
Yeah, let's go back.

01:21:37.590 --> 01:21:39.330
Time to swim, time to swim...

01:21:42.900 --> 01:21:43.590
Yeah!

01:21:57.100 --> 01:21:58.600
I'm sorry, sir!

01:21:59.430 --> 01:22:01.770
You guys have some nerve to skip practice.

01:22:01.770 --> 01:22:02.930
It was my fault!

01:22:03.310 --> 01:22:07.650
I ran out of school, and they all came after me because they were worried.

01:22:07.650 --> 01:22:10.110
That's why we were late for practice.

01:22:10.910 --> 01:22:12.110
I'm sorry, sir!

01:22:13.360 --> 01:22:15.830
I ran off without thinking about anything!

01:22:15.830 --> 01:22:17.120
I'm sorry, sir!

01:22:17.120 --> 01:22:19.640
I should've said something before going after them!

01:22:19.640 --> 01:22:21.060
I'm sorry, sir!

01:22:21.700 --> 01:22:24.210
Wh-What's the matter with you guys?

01:22:24.210 --> 01:22:25.680
Did you hit your heads or something?

01:22:25.680 --> 01:22:29.250
It's possible. Some idiot <i>did</i> tackle me.

01:22:29.250 --> 01:22:33.530
Th-That was... That was your fault for being confusing!

01:22:33.530 --> 01:22:35.710
I don't think people would normally get confused about that.

01:22:35.710 --> 01:22:37.430
What did you say?!

01:22:37.430 --> 01:22:39.790
Asahi, you really are a simpleton.

01:22:41.010 --> 01:22:42.430
Hey! Stop that!

01:22:43.140 --> 01:22:44.600
Let go!

01:22:48.340 --> 01:22:50.110
Bro, I've...

01:22:50.700 --> 01:22:54.330
been swimming in your shadow this whole time.

01:22:55.690 --> 01:22:57.900
But I'm going to stop now.

01:22:57.900 --> 01:22:59.990
And what you said before...

01:23:02.740 --> 01:23:04.450
I think I get it now.

01:23:06.040 --> 01:23:07.080
Ikuya.

01:23:09.030 --> 01:23:10.040
Oh yeah.

01:23:10.420 --> 01:23:11.790
Where's Nao?

01:23:12.710 --> 01:23:14.300
Oh, Nao?

01:23:14.300 --> 01:23:15.470
He's...

01:23:14.300 --> 01:23:16.300
Iwatobi
Hospital

01:23:16.790 --> 01:23:18.010
Nao!

01:23:18.570 --> 01:23:19.470
Guys.

01:23:19.760 --> 01:23:22.090
Nao, are you all right?

01:23:22.090 --> 01:23:25.510
Jeez, I told Natsuya not to say anything.

01:23:25.510 --> 01:23:27.560
But are you really all right, sir?

01:23:27.930 --> 01:23:30.090
We heard you were having surgery.

01:23:31.810 --> 01:23:33.920
It's not that big of a deal.

01:23:33.920 --> 01:23:36.040
And it looks like I'll get discharged right after.

01:23:37.900 --> 01:23:39.490
What kind of surgery are you having?

01:23:41.380 --> 01:23:42.760
It's to fix my detached retina.

01:23:44.140 --> 01:23:48.090
I'd been having a hard time seeing since last fall,

01:23:48.090 --> 01:23:51.150
but I thought it'd get better eventually and left it alone.

01:23:52.110 --> 01:23:54.760
In the end, I had to have surgery.

01:23:55.390 --> 01:23:56.210
When...

01:23:56.600 --> 01:23:59.720
When will you be able to return to practice?

01:24:00.450 --> 01:24:02.770
I can go back to coaching you guys right away.

01:24:04.100 --> 01:24:07.410
But I'll have to take a break from competing for a while.

01:24:09.910 --> 01:24:13.020
I won't be able to swim in any more races this year.

01:24:16.110 --> 01:24:19.070
Oh, hey, don't get all pessimistic.

01:24:19.590 --> 01:24:21.700
I won't be able to go to meets anymore in middle school,

01:24:22.110 --> 01:24:24.630
but I can still swim in high school.

01:24:25.780 --> 01:24:26.950
Will you keep swimming, sir?

01:24:28.600 --> 01:24:31.840
I started swimming when Natsuya pretty much forced me to join the swim club,

01:24:33.120 --> 01:24:35.130
but I really like it now.

01:24:37.800 --> 01:24:38.840
Asahi.

01:24:39.380 --> 01:24:43.290
When I was told that I wouldn't be able to compete anymore in middle school,

01:24:43.290 --> 01:24:44.600
I was really depressed.

01:24:45.300 --> 01:24:49.050
But I was able to feel better when I realized this wasn't the end.

01:24:49.050 --> 01:24:51.120
That there was no use being impatient.

01:24:51.120 --> 01:24:54.640
You'll also definitely be able to swim freestyle again.

01:24:54.640 --> 01:24:56.810
Just be patient, and do things without rushing.

01:24:56.810 --> 01:24:57.480
Yessir!

01:24:58.160 --> 01:25:00.740
Makoto, you worry about other people too much.

01:25:00.740 --> 01:25:03.300
You can be more selfish, you know.

01:25:03.300 --> 01:25:07.210
Also, I'm sure Haruka thinks you meddle too much.

01:25:07.210 --> 01:25:07.620
Huh?

01:25:08.020 --> 01:25:08.950
Really, Haru?

01:25:09.680 --> 01:25:12.680
Ikuya, trust those around you more.

01:25:12.680 --> 01:25:14.820
If you just stay inside your shell, it won't do you any good.

01:25:14.820 --> 01:25:17.260
That goes for both swimming and school.

01:25:18.500 --> 01:25:19.710
It's fine, sir.

01:25:20.160 --> 01:25:22.590
I kinda understand now.

01:25:25.110 --> 01:25:25.900
Glad to hear it.

01:25:27.290 --> 01:25:28.040
Haruka.

01:25:28.900 --> 01:25:29.640
Yes, sir.

01:25:30.330 --> 01:25:32.020
Stick to your convictions.

01:25:32.670 --> 01:25:35.300
You're swimming your beloved freestyle in the relay and individually, right?

01:25:36.070 --> 01:25:37.900
Don't be bound by the past.

01:25:38.370 --> 01:25:41.490
If you can, you'll be unbeatable.

01:25:43.420 --> 01:25:44.110
Right.

01:25:46.350 --> 01:25:52.090
I didn't want to do something lame like make my underclassmen shoulder my dreams,

01:25:53.430 --> 01:25:54.960
but since I can't swim,

01:25:56.100 --> 01:25:57.460
swim and win for me too.

01:25:58.750 --> 01:26:02.470
Serizawa Nao

01:25:59.150 --> 01:25:59.900
Yes, sir!

01:25:59.900 --> 01:26:02.470
Hey, not so loud!

01:26:04.220 --> 01:26:05.820
Let's run home!

01:26:05.820 --> 01:26:06.350
Huh?

01:26:06.350 --> 01:26:07.290
Run?

01:26:07.290 --> 01:26:10.580
I just feel like I've got all this energy pent up inside me!

01:26:10.580 --> 01:26:14.530
Just think of it as extra training and let's run!

01:26:13.260 --> 01:26:13.960
Hey!

01:26:13.960 --> 01:26:17.890
Jeez. This sorta thing is why meatheads are such a pain.

01:26:17.890 --> 01:26:19.920
Hey, wait!

01:26:19.920 --> 01:26:20.930
Haru!

01:26:48.930 --> 01:26:50.970
Yes! I won the—

01:26:53.030 --> 01:26:53.430
Haru?!

01:26:53.940 --> 01:26:54.930
Haru!

01:26:57.160 --> 01:26:57.650
Haru!

01:26:58.000 --> 01:26:58.980
Are you okay, Haru?!

01:26:59.390 --> 01:27:01.400
Hey, what's wrong? Do you feel sick?

01:27:01.670 --> 01:27:02.230
Haru!

01:27:02.760 --> 01:27:04.200
Get a hold of yourself, bro!

01:27:02.760 --> 01:27:07.450
<i>I said... to stop calling me... that...</i>

01:27:04.200 --> 01:27:05.150
C'mon!

01:27:05.150 --> 01:27:05.740
Haru!

01:27:05.740 --> 01:27:07.450
Snap out of it!

01:27:18.170 --> 01:27:20.190
What is it?

01:27:20.190 --> 01:27:22.040
Haru!

01:27:22.040 --> 01:27:24.280
It's because you're only eating mackerel!

01:27:24.280 --> 01:27:25.740
Don't make us worry!

01:27:25.740 --> 01:27:28.180
Haru, you passed out from low blood sugar.

01:27:28.890 --> 01:27:30.600
That's what the doctor said.

01:27:30.600 --> 01:27:32.480
Low blood sugar?

01:27:34.260 --> 01:27:36.810
Haru, you haven't been eating much, have you?

01:27:37.140 --> 01:27:39.510
You can't do that. You have to eat properly!

01:27:40.880 --> 01:27:41.690
I'm sorry.

01:27:41.690 --> 01:27:43.590
I was so worried.

01:27:45.470 --> 01:27:46.360
It's like...

01:27:47.690 --> 01:27:48.200
Yeah.

01:27:49.370 --> 01:27:51.970
So you're human too, huh, Haru?

01:27:51.970 --> 01:27:52.410
Huh?

01:27:54.570 --> 01:27:56.200
What're you talking about?

01:27:56.200 --> 01:27:58.540
Oh, you're awake?

01:27:58.540 --> 01:28:01.330
You can leave once that IV is finished.

01:28:01.950 --> 01:28:04.790
But you should take it easy for the rest of the day just in case.

01:28:04.790 --> 01:28:07.000
And make sure you eat enough.

01:28:07.000 --> 01:28:08.020
Yes, sir.

01:28:08.020 --> 01:28:11.800
Okay, I'll pay and then go grocery shopping.

01:28:12.110 --> 01:28:14.660
You boys take Haru home, okay?

01:28:14.660 --> 01:28:15.460
Okay.

01:28:42.210 --> 01:28:43.340
Haru!

01:28:43.340 --> 01:28:45.090
I brought over some food!

01:28:51.350 --> 01:28:53.140
Why are you all here?

01:28:53.460 --> 01:28:54.780
Here, you can have this!

01:28:54.780 --> 01:28:56.880
Excuse me!

01:28:56.880 --> 01:28:58.180
Excuse me.

01:28:59.370 --> 01:29:01.640
I'm gonna borrow your kitchen.

01:29:01.640 --> 01:29:02.690
Wait, why?

01:29:02.690 --> 01:29:06.690
This is all your fault for not taking care of yourself and passing out.

01:29:06.690 --> 01:29:11.870
So to make sure you don't get lazy and fall back on your bad eating habits,

01:29:11.870 --> 01:29:13.850
we'll be staying here for a while.

01:29:13.850 --> 01:29:14.740
What?

01:29:15.340 --> 01:29:18.240
Your mom said she'll be back in three days.

01:29:18.550 --> 01:29:20.810
So until then... Well, you should just suck it up.

01:29:20.810 --> 01:29:22.890
Oh, don't worry.

01:29:22.890 --> 01:29:25.840
We got the okay from everyone's parents,
including your mom.

01:29:26.250 --> 01:29:28.670
Just wait in the living room.

01:29:29.320 --> 01:29:30.760
What about my okay?

01:29:30.760 --> 01:29:33.080
Asahi, you're in the way there. Move.

01:29:33.080 --> 01:29:34.190
Oh, sorry.

01:29:34.190 --> 01:29:35.470
Wait, what're you doing?

01:29:35.850 --> 01:29:38.640
Why are you cutting it before peeling it, you idiot?

01:29:38.640 --> 01:29:40.460
What are you doing?

01:29:40.460 --> 01:29:41.730
All the pieces are shaped weirdly.

01:29:41.730 --> 01:29:42.930
You're terrible at it!

01:29:44.720 --> 01:29:45.810
It's overflowing!

01:29:45.810 --> 01:29:47.360
Hot!

01:29:47.360 --> 01:29:48.750
That's dangerous!

01:29:48.750 --> 01:29:50.230
Sorry.

01:29:53.490 --> 01:29:56.810
This is what we made, and this is from my mom.

01:29:56.810 --> 01:29:57.940
Now, let's eat.

01:29:57.940 --> 01:29:59.450
Thanks for the food!

01:29:59.450 --> 01:30:00.580
Thanks for the food.

01:30:01.180 --> 01:30:02.290
Here, Haru.

01:30:16.720 --> 01:30:18.540
How is it? Any good?

01:30:19.160 --> 01:30:20.230
It's not bad.

01:30:21.270 --> 01:30:23.720
Why're you hiding how you really feel?

01:30:23.720 --> 01:30:24.910
You are too.

01:30:24.910 --> 01:30:25.910
Did you say something?

01:30:25.910 --> 01:30:26.900
Nope, nothing.

01:30:26.900 --> 01:30:29.610
Besides, you always act without thinking, Asahi!

01:30:29.940 --> 01:30:31.390
You're such a child!

01:30:31.390 --> 01:30:33.070
Not to mention your little misunderstanding.

01:30:33.070 --> 01:30:34.220
What?

01:30:34.220 --> 01:30:36.620
You're the one who was crying like a baby!

01:30:36.620 --> 01:30:37.230
Wh—

01:30:37.230 --> 01:30:38.490
Th-That's not...

01:30:38.490 --> 01:30:41.200
That's not what happened at all!

01:30:41.560 --> 01:30:43.050
Oh yeah? Oh yeah?

01:30:43.050 --> 01:30:44.210
Why are you talking weird?

01:30:44.210 --> 01:30:46.290
Come on, stop that.

01:30:47.400 --> 01:30:48.210
He laughed!

01:30:48.540 --> 01:30:49.090
No, I didn't.

01:30:49.090 --> 01:30:51.910
No, I saw it! You definitely laughed just now!

01:30:51.910 --> 01:30:53.010
I saw it too!

01:30:53.010 --> 01:30:54.050
You saw nothing.

01:30:54.050 --> 01:30:55.620
I definitely saw it.

01:30:55.620 --> 01:30:58.990
I guess you can be adorable sometimes too, huh?

01:30:58.990 --> 01:31:00.810
Shut up and eat.

01:31:03.300 --> 01:31:05.650
It's like an overnight school trip.

01:31:05.650 --> 01:31:07.280
Hurry up and go to sleep.

01:31:07.280 --> 01:31:07.970
You're too loud.

01:31:07.970 --> 01:31:10.110
Don't act like you're my parent.

01:31:10.110 --> 01:31:11.690
I just can't sleep!

01:31:12.090 --> 01:31:14.320
We have school tomorrow too.

01:31:16.490 --> 01:31:19.390
I feel like swimming right now!

01:31:20.740 --> 01:31:24.120
Even though you looked like you were dying every time you swam until just recently?

01:31:29.090 --> 01:31:30.200
I feel like...

01:31:31.110 --> 01:31:32.290
I'll be okay now!

01:31:32.780 --> 01:31:33.790
Huh?

01:31:33.790 --> 01:31:37.050
Like, the second I saw Haru's freestyle, I thought,

01:31:37.550 --> 01:31:42.850
"There's a guy who's way, way better than me,"
and it seemed like it really sunk in.

01:31:44.140 --> 01:31:45.930
And after thinking about a lot of stuff,

01:31:46.580 --> 01:31:48.810
I've started to feel like he really is better than me.

01:31:49.540 --> 01:31:51.980
How did that help you recover?

01:31:51.980 --> 01:31:53.820
When I saw Haru pass out today,

01:31:54.350 --> 01:31:57.760
I realized that he's just a regular human too.

01:31:57.760 --> 01:31:59.320
Isn't that obvious?

01:32:03.410 --> 01:32:06.260
I guess I have a lot pride,

01:32:06.260 --> 01:32:09.870
but looking at that part of Haru made me feel a lot better.

01:32:10.270 --> 01:32:13.130
I felt like I could accept myself even if I'm not that good.

01:32:14.720 --> 01:32:19.090
However, I can't just let Haru keep beating me!

01:32:19.380 --> 01:32:20.970
I'll definitely beat you one day!

01:32:22.930 --> 01:32:23.850
Do what you want.

01:32:23.850 --> 01:32:26.000
You bet I will!

01:32:26.000 --> 01:32:28.680
Well, it's nice to know you at
least thought one thing through.

01:32:28.680 --> 01:32:29.890
Are you making fun of me?

01:32:29.890 --> 01:32:31.030
Now, now.

01:32:31.030 --> 01:32:34.650
But it's actually amazing that you can self-reflect like that.

01:32:35.120 --> 01:32:37.160
Self-reflect...

01:32:38.470 --> 01:32:42.320
But I think you should start by carefully self-reflecting.

01:32:43.440 --> 01:32:44.940
Oh, I see.

01:32:44.940 --> 01:32:47.470
So that's what he meant.

01:32:47.470 --> 01:32:48.390
Who?

01:32:48.390 --> 01:32:51.470
There was a guy who gave me advice at the library.

01:32:51.470 --> 01:32:52.210
What was he like?

01:32:52.210 --> 01:32:53.430
He wore glasses!

01:32:53.430 --> 01:32:54.960
What? That's it?

01:32:55.300 --> 01:32:57.950
How are we supposed to know what he's like with just that?

01:33:02.290 --> 01:33:03.760
In elementary school,

01:33:03.760 --> 01:33:07.500
Haru and I took part in an amazing medley relay.

01:33:07.500 --> 01:33:08.430
Makoto.

01:33:09.070 --> 01:33:10.810
At Iwatobi SC?

01:33:12.840 --> 01:33:13.550
Yeah.

01:33:13.550 --> 01:33:14.900
Our teammates were this kid Nagisa,

01:33:15.770 --> 01:33:17.790
and another kid named Rin.

01:33:17.790 --> 01:33:20.370
You might remember hearing about him at the practice swim meet.

01:33:20.370 --> 01:33:23.820
I thought back then that was the best team I'd swim with in my whole life.

01:33:24.330 --> 01:33:25.870
And we did win.

01:33:26.420 --> 01:33:30.140
But then we graduated,
and everyone suddenly became separated.

01:33:30.990 --> 01:33:33.250
I didn't believe I could be on a team better than that, so...

01:33:33.870 --> 01:33:36.880
So I wasn't very optimistic about the relay.

01:33:38.210 --> 01:33:40.300
I don't know if it means anything coming from me,

01:33:40.300 --> 01:33:44.850
but I noticed that the two of you
weren't really serious about the relay.

01:33:47.200 --> 01:33:47.970
Sorry.

01:33:48.910 --> 01:33:49.810
I don't get it.

01:33:51.330 --> 01:33:55.480
If it was such a great team,
then why are you being all negative about it?

01:33:55.810 --> 01:33:58.550
I'll feel bad for them if you talk like that.

01:33:58.550 --> 01:34:00.690
It's fine if that team's the best.

01:34:00.690 --> 01:34:03.450
But that's not fair to you two.

01:34:03.450 --> 01:34:04.610
Why not?

01:34:04.610 --> 01:34:08.910
I think the relay team at my old SC was the best too!

01:34:09.280 --> 01:34:13.000
But I want to make the best team here too!

01:34:15.290 --> 01:34:17.000
Makoto, Haru.

01:34:17.000 --> 01:34:18.710
It's no use trying to reason with an idiot.

01:34:19.140 --> 01:34:20.550
Are you picking a fight?!

01:34:21.550 --> 01:34:24.040
I thought that I was fine as long as I could swim by myself.

01:34:24.040 --> 01:34:26.880
That I just needed to get a personal best.

01:34:26.880 --> 01:34:31.490
But now, I want to swim a relay with this team.

01:35:16.980 --> 01:35:18.350
Mackerel Acqua Pazza

01:36:19.960 --> 01:36:21.790
It's finally time for the official meet.

01:36:21.790 --> 01:36:25.490
Your times today will guide you for the rest of the year.

01:36:25.490 --> 01:36:26.620
Give it your all.

01:36:26.620 --> 01:36:27.380
Yes, sir!

01:36:28.060 --> 01:36:29.600
Let's do this, Iwatobi Middle School!

01:36:29.600 --> 01:36:31.010
Yeah!

01:36:31.290 --> 01:36:32.460
Ready...

01:36:33.420 --> 01:36:34.390
Go!

01:36:34.860 --> 01:36:35.980
Well, here I go!

01:36:35.980 --> 01:36:36.650
Okay!

01:36:41.350 --> 01:36:44.860
Iwatobi Middle School

01:36:41.920 --> 01:36:43.360
The relay's coming up soon.

01:36:43.360 --> 01:36:44.860
How's it going? Think you can do it?

01:36:45.420 --> 01:36:45.960
Yessir!

01:36:45.960 --> 01:36:47.360
Yes, sir.

01:36:48.410 --> 01:36:49.190
What about you, Haruka?

01:36:50.020 --> 01:36:55.030
The relay we swam in elementary school was really special to me and Makoto.

01:36:55.540 --> 01:37:00.370
That's why I didn't want to swim a relay with any other team.

01:37:00.370 --> 01:37:01.290
And?

01:37:02.220 --> 01:37:04.410
But now things have changed a little.

01:37:05.800 --> 01:37:08.300
I want to swim a relay with this team right now.

01:37:12.680 --> 01:37:13.380
Good.

01:37:13.380 --> 01:37:14.390
Do your best.

01:37:14.390 --> 01:37:20.770
Iwatobi Middle School

01:37:14.870 --> 01:37:16.520
Make sure you win!

01:37:16.520 --> 01:37:17.150
Yes, sir!

01:37:17.150 --> 01:37:18.800
All right, let's go!

01:37:18.800 --> 01:37:20.770
You'll trip if you get carried away, idiot.

01:37:23.220 --> 01:37:26.940
It's because there are moments like this that I can never stop coaching.

01:37:27.950 --> 01:37:31.900
That's fine, but hurry up and come back as a competitor.

01:37:32.340 --> 01:37:33.950
I'm getting tired of waiting.

01:37:34.990 --> 01:37:35.950
I'll be back someday.

01:37:44.750 --> 01:37:48.860
I hope you guys don't do another
half-assed swim like you did the other day.

01:37:49.920 --> 01:37:52.670
Boys' Locker Room

01:37:50.650 --> 01:37:51.880
I won't lose.

01:37:59.540 --> 01:38:01.270
Oh, it's Haru's team!

01:38:08.330 --> 01:38:13.450
We will now have the boys' 400m medley relay.

01:38:14.860 --> 01:38:16.420
Makoto, you can do it!

01:38:16.420 --> 01:38:17.790
We're leaving the start to you!

01:38:17.790 --> 01:38:18.370
Right!

01:38:22.570 --> 01:38:23.730
Ready...

01:38:27.210 --> 01:38:28.000
Go!

01:38:31.380 --> 01:38:32.840
All right! It's a great start!

01:38:33.210 --> 01:38:34.680
You've got this, Makoto!

01:38:34.680 --> 01:38:40.860
Go, go, go, go, go, Makoto!

01:38:40.860 --> 01:38:43.270
Swim, swim, swim, swim, swim, Makoto!

01:38:43.270 --> 01:38:44.350
Tachibana!

01:38:44.350 --> 01:38:45.230
You can do it!

01:38:45.860 --> 01:38:47.190
Makoto's in front!

01:38:47.190 --> 01:38:49.730
Go, Mako!

01:38:57.950 --> 01:38:58.700
He's fast.

01:39:00.830 --> 01:39:04.000
Hey, don't lose the vontage Makoto got for us.

01:39:05.140 --> 01:39:07.010
Who do you think you're talking to?

01:39:07.010 --> 01:39:11.400
Also, it "advantage," you idiot.

01:39:14.680 --> 01:39:15.970
Ikuya!

01:39:27.810 --> 01:39:30.690
He's gotten better.

01:39:31.390 --> 01:39:33.860
Go, Ikuya!

01:39:43.820 --> 01:39:45.830
Go for it, Ikuya!

01:39:45.830 --> 01:39:47.750
Asahi, you can do it!

01:39:47.750 --> 01:39:49.580
Just swim right back here.

01:39:50.070 --> 01:39:51.460
Haru, Makoto.

01:39:52.340 --> 01:39:55.210
I'm happy I'm swimming with this team.

01:39:55.750 --> 01:39:57.470
It's really fun!

01:39:57.470 --> 01:39:58.510
Thanks.

01:40:08.410 --> 01:40:10.190
Asahi!

01:40:11.770 --> 01:40:13.800
Asahi, go!

01:40:13.800 --> 01:40:15.480
Hurry up and get back here, idiot!

01:40:15.920 --> 01:40:18.200
Asahi's start got better too.

01:40:18.200 --> 01:40:19.740
He's completely in sync with you.

01:40:20.820 --> 01:40:21.990
Not that I want that.

01:40:28.070 --> 01:40:29.080
Oh?

01:40:29.400 --> 01:40:30.330
Not bad.

01:40:35.460 --> 01:40:36.320
Haru.

01:40:36.320 --> 01:40:39.090
Haru, we'll be waiting here for you.

01:40:39.540 --> 01:40:40.210
Yeah.

01:40:47.890 --> 01:40:50.060
Haruka!

01:40:53.190 --> 01:40:59.070
Go, go, go, go, go, Haruka!

01:40:59.070 --> 01:41:01.910
Swim, swim, swim, swim, swim, Haruka!

01:41:11.040 --> 01:41:13.420
Haru!

01:41:27.050 --> 01:41:27.950
Haru!

01:41:42.150 --> 01:41:44.070
Haru!

01:41:44.550 --> 01:41:45.780
That was the best!

01:41:46.070 --> 01:41:47.280
It was amazing!

01:41:46.070 --> 01:41:48.790
Yes! We did it!

01:41:51.090 --> 01:41:53.490
Look! We got first!

01:41:51.090 --> 01:41:52.210
Amazing!

01:41:52.210 --> 01:41:53.960
We won!

01:41:53.960 --> 01:41:54.730
We got first!

01:41:54.730 --> 01:41:56.280
We did it!

01:41:56.280 --> 01:41:57.040
We're...

01:41:59.050 --> 01:42:00.800
Yes, yes, yes!

01:42:04.430 --> 01:42:07.050
Amazing! That was amazing!

01:42:25.690 --> 01:42:26.910
<i>Dear Sousuke.</i>

01:42:28.150 --> 01:42:29.560
<i>How are you?</i>

01:42:29.560 --> 01:42:31.850
<i>I'm all right, I guess.</i>

01:42:31.850 --> 01:42:34.040
<i>I've finally gotten used to living here.</i>

01:42:34.650 --> 01:42:37.420
<i>At first, there was the language barrier,</i>

01:42:37.420 --> 01:42:42.760
<i>so I did my best with gestures and pictures, but no one understood me!</i>

01:42:42.760 --> 01:42:46.320
<i>Like one day, I drew a picture of a cherry tree,
and someone brought me a mop.</i>

01:42:46.320 --> 01:42:49.300
<i>It really made me want to go back to Japan.</i>

01:42:49.940 --> 01:42:52.870
<i>And there are kangaroos just on the street!</i>

01:42:52.870 --> 01:42:56.850
<i>I wanted to touch them,
but I was told not to because they kick.</i>

01:42:57.380 --> 01:43:00.310
<i>Everyone at the swimming club here is fast.</i>

01:43:00.860 --> 01:43:02.730
<i>I lose every day.</i>

01:43:03.120 --> 01:43:06.070
<i>I wish I could say that I win every day,</i>

01:43:06.590 --> 01:43:09.200
<i>but everyone's bigger than Makoto,</i>

01:43:09.870 --> 01:43:11.540
<i>and I can feel the difference in power.</i>

01:43:12.650 --> 01:43:15.560
<i>I got put in the slowest class for now.</i>

01:43:16.250 --> 01:43:18.490
<i>I feel frustrated every day.</i>

01:43:19.890 --> 01:43:21.460
<i>Maybe I'll get used to it eventually,</i>

01:43:21.870 --> 01:43:24.860
<i>and what frustrates me now will stop feeling frustrating.</i>

01:43:25.740 --> 01:43:27.380
<i>That's a scary thought.</i>

01:43:28.690 --> 01:43:30.830
<i>But I'll never give up!</i>

01:43:30.830 --> 01:43:32.430
<i>I'll definitely get faster!</i>

01:43:32.430 --> 01:43:33.560
<i>Faster than anyone!</i>

01:43:34.420 --> 01:43:38.440
<i>I haven't forgotten a thing about that relay.</i>

01:43:39.570 --> 01:43:43.190
<i>Even now, that guy swims in front of me.</i>

01:43:44.030 --> 01:43:46.840
<i>I want to swim like he does.</i>

01:43:48.320 --> 01:43:50.950
<i>I want to hurry up and be able to swim like Haru!</i>

01:43:52.950 --> 01:43:54.750
Even now, that guy swims in front of me.

01:43:52.950 --> 01:43:54.750
I want to swim like he does. I want to hurry up and be able to swim like Haru!

01:43:55.750 --> 01:43:57.120
Even now, that guy swims in front of me.

01:43:55.750 --> 01:43:57.120
I want to swim like he does. I want to hurry up and be able to swim like Haru!

01:43:59.090 --> 01:43:59.880
<i>Rin.</i>

01:44:01.250 --> 01:44:02.000
<i>I do too.</i>

01:44:03.310 --> 01:44:04.120
<i>I want to...</i>

01:44:05.710 --> 01:44:07.250
<i>swim like you too.</i>

01:44:08.450 --> 01:44:10.790
That letter was addressed to you.

01:44:13.670 --> 01:44:15.150
It was to you, wasn't it?

01:44:15.150 --> 01:44:16.980
Look at it carefully.

01:44:16.980 --> 01:44:19.940
The part where he wrote "he does" was erased.

01:44:19.940 --> 01:44:23.060
Even now, that guy swims in front of me.

01:44:19.940 --> 01:44:23.060
I want to swim like he does. I want to hurry up and be able to swim like Haru!

01:44:20.850 --> 01:44:23.060
It's faint, but it used to say "you do."

01:44:24.070 --> 01:44:28.780
like he does. I want

01:44:25.670 --> 01:44:29.910
Knowing Rin, he was probably going
to send it to you but got embarrassed,

01:44:29.910 --> 01:44:33.530
but since he went through the trouble of writing it,
he sent it to me instead.

01:44:35.590 --> 01:44:36.540
He <i>would</i> do that.

01:44:36.540 --> 01:44:38.040
like he does. I want

01:44:40.090 --> 01:44:42.600
When I read it, I thought it was weird.

01:44:42.600 --> 01:44:44.800
Especially since he mentioned Tachibana.

01:44:45.310 --> 01:44:47.300
More than anything, the writing was too one-sided.

01:44:48.010 --> 01:44:50.930
It was like he wasn't expecting an answer.

01:44:51.850 --> 01:44:55.770
Knowing my personality,
he wouldn't have written it like that to me.

01:44:57.590 --> 01:44:59.140
I'll let you keep that letter.

01:44:59.140 --> 01:44:59.940
Really?

01:45:00.580 --> 01:45:03.100
I'm pretty sure that's what Rin would've wanted me to do.

01:45:03.100 --> 01:45:04.850
I'll beat you in the individual event next time.

01:45:04.850 --> 01:45:05.440
Later.

01:45:09.160 --> 01:45:10.450
Haru!

01:45:12.420 --> 01:45:13.870
Let's go home!

01:45:15.750 --> 01:45:16.550
Yeah.

01:45:25.810 --> 01:45:31.310
The sky bathed all the clouds in a glow

01:45:31.310 --> 01:45:34.610
As they drifted through the heavens

01:45:34.610 --> 01:45:39.500
And I heard a howling squall

01:45:39.500 --> 01:45:46.860
As if a scream filled my mind

01:46:05.140 --> 01:46:10.580
One day I came to understand

01:46:10.580 --> 01:46:13.930
That the tears streaming down

01:46:13.930 --> 01:46:18.770
My fever-tinged face

01:46:18.770 --> 01:46:24.960
Were the amalgamation of all my pain

01:46:24.960 --> 01:46:27.240
One day I gazed

01:46:27.240 --> 01:46:29.400
At my clenched fist

01:46:29.400 --> 01:46:33.750
Thinking of all the shit I've been through

01:46:33.750 --> 01:46:35.750
Deep inside of

01:46:35.750 --> 01:46:38.080
A single breath of mine

01:46:38.080 --> 01:46:44.540
I've been burned before, so hold me back

01:46:44.540 --> 01:46:49.030
Where is the blue that we got to fly?

01:46:49.030 --> 01:46:55.340
As we set our sights on our shining tomorrow

01:46:55.340 --> 01:47:02.060
We shared in each other's skies

01:47:02.060 --> 01:47:06.540
Where is the light that we want to dive?

01:47:06.540 --> 01:47:10.860
As we head toward the future that we had once lost

01:47:10.860 --> 01:47:18.250
Even if our hands drift apart, we'll still have

01:47:18.250 --> 01:47:21.760
The place where we're firmly tied

01:47:30.220 --> 01:47:35.630
When unrealized aspirations pushed me to anger

01:47:35.630 --> 01:47:38.840
I kicked out in frustation

01:47:38.840 --> 01:47:43.820
And as I closed my eyes to it

01:47:43.820 --> 01:47:48.020
My dream was torn away into the wind

01:47:48.020 --> 01:47:50.130
Someday you will

01:47:50.130 --> 01:47:52.340
Drop your fist down

01:47:52.340 --> 01:47:56.700
On all the memories you've inherited

01:47:56.700 --> 01:47:58.670
Inside and out

01:47:58.670 --> 01:48:01.020
But I don't know why

01:48:01.020 --> 01:48:07.560
You try to give it all up, but we hold you back

01:48:07.560 --> 01:48:11.900
Where is the blue that we got to fly?

01:48:11.900 --> 01:48:16.340
The tomorrow we were holding above us

01:48:16.340 --> 01:48:20.480
Passed right by

01:48:20.480 --> 01:48:24.980
Among the hesitation of familiar days

01:48:24.980 --> 01:48:29.420
Where is the light that we want to dive?

01:48:29.420 --> 01:48:33.730
As we were chasing after our future

01:48:33.730 --> 01:48:41.210
Our foolish detours brought us right to

01:48:41.210 --> 01:48:44.730
The place where we're truly known

01:49:06.680 --> 01:49:13.400
Go, make our way

01:49:09.620 --> 01:49:14.170
I just grab the ache and go to the other side

01:49:13.400 --> 01:49:23.310
Hold it tight

01:49:14.170 --> 01:49:18.460
Nothing has worked to cool your anger down

01:49:18.460 --> 01:49:21.880
Though I saw the star on your back

01:49:23.990 --> 01:49:30.750
Go, gaze our sight

01:49:27.080 --> 01:49:31.640
I just grab the ache and go to the other side

01:49:30.750 --> 01:49:39.380
It will surely resound

01:49:31.640 --> 01:49:36.040
Nothing has worked to cool your anger down

01:49:36.040 --> 01:49:39.380
All I wanted was the horns

01:49:39.380 --> 01:49:43.630
Where is the blue that we got to fly?

01:49:43.630 --> 01:49:47.950
With our unshakeable resolve

01:49:47.950 --> 01:49:52.110
We should be able to forge a path

01:49:52.110 --> 01:49:56.610
To our shining tomorrow

01:49:56.610 --> 01:50:01.090
Where is the light that we want to dive?

01:50:01.090 --> 01:50:05.380
Our future has long been out of our grasps

01:50:05.380 --> 01:50:12.770
But now that we hold it firmly in our hands we can reach

01:50:12.770 --> 01:50:16.200
The place where we really shine
